{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/648872-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-8","id":648872,"title":"Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga (Actual Play) Part 8","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-02T06:50:50-07:00","id":648872,"title":"Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga (Actual Play) Part 8","content":"The Kiddie Pool Saga Continues!<br /> <br /> Previous Chapters and Character Portraits can be found here [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\">LINK</a>]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>It's Not Paranoia if They're Really Out to Get You</u></b><br /> <br /> Ever since the night Alice and I saw Seville's Nosferatu chasing down and executing a rogue vampire on the orders of the Prince, we have stepped up our efforts to ferret out traitors. Alice has spent a lot of time looking into the minds of newcomers for the slightest sign of disloyalty.<br /> <br /> I have joined in, using my Dominate to question newcomers and then erasing their memory of it. It is distasteful, I know. However, if I am to take on the responsibilities of the Mekhetocracy then I must use all tools at my disposal. Whenever possible, I have had a mekhet observer present during questioning (in addition to Alice) in an effort to maintain my reputation for integrity.<br /> <br /> Anyway, one night we tag teamed Abigail Taft (daeva, carthian) with the Auspex/Dominate interrogation and something kinda crazy happened. I looked into Abigail's eyes for signs of mental tampering... and rolled 17 successes on my Dominate roll. In doing so, I unlocked some memories which had apparently been buried deep by another practictioner of Dominate. Here is what we learned:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Abigail is the childe of Ferdinand (mekhet, older neonate, invictus, former hound.)<br /> 2. The memory of her true origins have been hidden from her.<br /> 3. She has been programmed to seek out those who would attempt to overthrow the Prince and aid them.<br /> <br /> I have heard rumors of the lengths to which the mekhetocracy will go to ferret out sedition, but this is ridiculous. I do my best to put her back the way I found her, but make it a point to talk to my Grandsire about this. My current belief is that a member of my family did this at the order of the Prince, but it never hurts to check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Status Report</u></b><br /> <br /> In the time since the last write-up, there have been some changes to the status quo. Council Territory, which lies to the south and east of Baltimore, has fallen to the Werewolves. I don't know how many of the resident vampires remain there, how many have fled, nor how many have met their final end in the conflict.<br /> <br /> Closer to home some of the younger vampires have been recruited by some of the older ones:<br /> <br /> 1. Terry the Mekhet has been recruited into the organization of Michael Seville. She continues to make her haven in my Cousin Antony's territory and pay him corvee for the privilege, but her loyalty is ultimately with Michael Seville and the Carthians.<br /> <br /> 2. Eve Liebsch (gangrel): Eve has been a resident of the kiddy pool since the very beginning of the game. Since that time, she had been wanting to find for herself a sponsor into the First Estate. For whatever reason, she never found one. Michael Seville has recently convinced her to give up her ambitions in favor of membership in the Carthian Movement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Delegation</u></b><br /> <br /> Well, Alice and I consider Antony's allowing Terry to slip through his fingers to be a serious failure. even though we have discussed the matter with him once before, we decide to speak with him again. One of the reasons we are a bit upset about it is, we probably would have recruited Terry into our line of fealty had we not believed that Antony had his sights on her.<br /> <br /> So, we arrive at Antony's bar but discover that we have to wait our turn. Antony is already having a meeting with the Archon Helen (mekhet, ancilla, crone.) The door to Antony's office opens, and both he and Helen approach us.<br /> <br /> <b>Helen:</b> &quot;Oh, what serendipity. I can delegate a task to you. Are you familiar with Pedro?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pedro is a gangrel and a member of the Circle. We have attended some of his 'observances' in the past (some of you may remember that just such an event was used to sour Felicity on the idea of joining the Circle.) Anyway, Pedro has a pair of goat skin pants that he wears when conducting ceremonies. Well, it has become something of a game amongst residents of the Quarantine Zone to steal Pedro's pants. The last time Pedro's pants went missing, Cooper (daeva, almoner, sadist) recovered them and returned them to Pedro in exchange for a boon.<br /> <br /> So, Helen explains to us that Pedro's pants have gone missing again, but this time Pedro has raised the issue with Appolonia (daeva priscus, priestess of the Crone.)<br /> <br /> <b>Helen:</b> &quot;Please see to the return of the property to its rightful owner and identify the thief. We need a sacrifice for next month's festivities.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><u>Finger Wagging</u></b><br /> <br /> Helen leaves and we begin our conversation with Antony. We tell him again that we are disappointed with his failure to seal the deal with Terry. We are worried that perhaps he is too narrow minded and unwilling to sign a long term service deal with someone who is not Invictus. We even point to Kat (gangrel, carthian) with whom we have made a service arrangement.<br /> <br /> Antony counters that while it is true that their difference in covenant is in fact the reason he did not recruit her more aggressively, his motivation was not snobbery. It was order. Round pegs belong in round holes. Terry is Carthian. She belongs with Seville.<br /> <br /> <b>Antony</b> (changing the subject): &quot;Helen has asked me to host an official City Court, here in my bar later this week. There are several minor grievances which will be arbitrated for the members of the Quarantine Zone. I'd like you two to be on hand in case there is any trouble.&quot;<br /> <br /> We agree to be there, of course. This certainly fits into our duties as Marshals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Care and Feeding of Ghouls</u></b><br /> <br /> The two of us head across the bay to the Quarantine Zone and begin asking questions about Pedro's missing pants. After asking around, we get a tip that a ghoul named 'Blood' belonging to Trenton (i've met the guy... like once. So many unfamiliar vampires running around these days.) has the pants.<br /> <br /> Alice and I look for Trenton inside the Jiffy Lube where vampires of the QZ like to socialize. When we arrive, we are approached by Shaman. Shaman asks Alice and I for a private word and we follow him upstairs. Shaman wants advice from us about how to take custody of a ghoul away from another vampire by way of the Baltimore legal system.<br /> <br /> Apparently, the very public way in which I stole Caroline (daeva) from Fitzgerald (daeva, deceased) is not a secret even amongst the newcomers of the QZ. (I wrote about this way back in part 1, if memory serves.) Well, I am not in the habit of giving legal advice, but I do ask him for more information. Shaman wants to steal Snow (ghoul of Getter) and take her for his own.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;Snow has a big heart. Before we came to join Baltimore, Getter asked Mortimer (nosferatu from Council Territory) to find him a good candidate to be made a ghoul, and Mortimer found Snow. When he moved here, Getter saw that one of the only vampires doing well financially was Fishy&quot; (Fishy [daeva] makes her money and gets her meals via prostitution)<br /> <br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;Getter wanted Snow to do what Fishy was doing and bring him the money, but Snow refused. Well, Getter doesn't have the right powers to control her directly. So, he started withholding the blood. Snow was allowed to lapse back to mortal and made ghoul again several times but still refused to whore for Getter. She turned to drugs to ease the pain of withdrawl from vitae. She doesn't deserve to be treated that way.&quot;<br /> <br /> I gave Shaman the best advice I could think of: &quot;Stay away from the courts. They are dangerous.&quot; However, something tells me Getter is not long for this world. He will slip up. When he does, I will bring her to him rather than disposing of her. Shaman agrees that he will owe me a boon if that should come to pass.<br /> <br /> I should mention a cultural difference between the Vampires of the Council and those of Baltimore as regards the treatment of ghouls. Due to the fact that there has been an ongoing conflict with werewolves and the council, council vampires die with more regularity than do citizens of Baltimore. Further, the Council has a less well developed infrastructure for the preservation of the Masquerade. As a result, when a vampire dies the final death their ghouls are more likely to be adopted by other vampires rather than to be murdered and cremated as tends to happen in Baltimore. (It's important to stop the spread of cooties.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Gone Fishin</u></b><br /> <br /> We left the Jiffy Lube and soon found Trenton. There was a brief conversation in which we inquired as to the whereabouts of the goat skin pants. I tell him that we have heard his ghoul has the pants, and that a citizen of Baltimore has made a complaint. We further tell him that if the pants do not find their way into our hands, there will be trouble.<br /> <br /> Trenton agrees to retreive the pants. Alice and I make it clear that this is not in any way an exchange of boons, and Trenton leaves. Not satisfied to take a hands off approach, Alice and I follow him under cloak of Obfuscate. Trenton travels to the north end of the Quarantine Zone near the water.<br /> <br /> There is a small shack and a boat launch. On the door to the shack is a hastily written sign, &quot;Gone Fishin.&quot; Trenton finds a place to sit and wait. Alice and I do the same. In about 2 hours a small boat arrives, apparently from across the bay. Two ghouls disembark from the boat, one of whom is Blood. Trenton approaches the duo and dismisses the unnamed ghoul.<br /> <br /> <b>Trenton:</b> &quot;Do you have the pants?&quot;<br /> <b>Blood:</b> &quot;Yeah. You interested? I'll give them to you, and you'll owe me a boon and stuff.&quot;<br /> <b>Trenton:</b> &quot;Are you fucking stupid?&quot; *SMACK*<br /> <b>Blood:</b> &quot;What the fuck?&quot;<br /> <b>Trenton:</b> *SMACK*<br /> <br /> Blood runs into the shack and returns with a box which presumably contains Pedro's pants. I step out of the shadows and take the box. Alice remains invisible (which she often does.) I open the box to confirm the contents, which for some reason have been spray painted gold, while Alice does her patented Mekhet telepathy maneuver. Here is what she learned:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Blood is not the ghoul of Trenton. He used to be the ghoul of Charles Wood (recently deceased.) Blood has thus far been unable to find a new regnant. However, a vampire from Council Territory (Nick) has been arranging feedings for him in exchange for favors. I don't know why Nick would want Blood to sell Pedro's pants, but ... whatever.<br /> <br /> This is precisely the reason the city makes you ask permission to create ghouls. In the event that you should meet your final death, they want to know who all your ghouls are so they can be rounded up, rather than become little random elements running around willing to do anything to get another taste of that sweet sweet vitae.<br /> <br /> 2. The other ghoul in the boat was named Sara, and she belongs to a nosferatu named Broom.<br /> <br /> I thank Trenton for his cooperation and head for home.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Home is Where the Heart is</u></b><br /> <br /> We arrive at home to spend the last few hours before dawn to find we have a visitor. My eldest Cousin Rosalyn Burnett is here. Rosalyn is a member of Invictus and is the sire of Susan Small. She is also very uptight, which is the reason I greet her with a warm embrace and kiss on each cheek. She hands me an envelope containing an invitation to the next family dinner. It is set to happen tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> In spite of the short notice given for the gathering, all members of the family arrived at the Von Berg estate at the appointed time. Per usual, there is a bit of small talk and mingling before the doors to the dining room are opened. We arrange ourselves at the table according to age, with my uncles and aunt closest to the head of the table where Konrad, our Patriarch, sits.<br /> <br /> There is a long silence. Septimus has an expression on his face as though he is chewing on particularly sour lemons. My cousin Sandy breaks the silence.<br /> <br /> <b>Sandy:</b> &quot;Well... What's going on?&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus:</b> &quot;There has been a change in the family, and there is no need to keep you in suspense. Octavia has decided to leave the covenant of Invictus.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are some surprised looks on the faces around the table. None more than Christina (Octavia's childe) who looks like she might even cry.<br /> <br /> <b>Octavia:</b> &quot;I will of course relinquish all holdings that I procured during my tenure with the Invictus.&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus:</b> &quot;Yes, we will have to divide your lands and holdings and make sure everyone is well bribed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Septimus continues to explain how many Invictus vampires will need to be given pieces of the pie to maintain the balance of power in the city. (ie: maintain the size of Invictus lands) He elaborates that people who have sworn their fealty to Octavia will be given the opportunity to be relieved of their obligations.<br /> <br /> <b>Konrad:</b> &quot;No. The balance will be maintained. Invictus holdings with remain in Invictus hands and Ventrue holdings will remain in Ventrue hands.<br /> <br /> Septimus begins to protest but he is interrupted again.<br /> <br /> <b>Konrad:</b> &quot;No. We will not give up our holdings. We will not give up any territories. We will not give up any money. If anyone has a problem with this arrangement, we will fight.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;So, are we here then to make battle plans and contingencies?&quot;<br /> <b>Konrad:</b> &quot;I have already made them, which you will see soon enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Guess Who's Coming to Dinner</u></b><br /> <br /> With that, dinner is served and in about an hour there is a knock on the door. Helen (mekhet, archon, circle) is admitted into the house.<br /> <br /> <b>Helen:</b> &quot;He has been informed. I am His eyes and ears.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not long after, there is another knock. This time several vampires are admitted into the house:<br /> <br /> <b>Michael Seville</b> (nosferatu priscus, carthian)<br /> <b>Boris</b> (nosferatu, ancilla, circle)<br /> <b>Spider</b> (nosferatu, childe of Boris)<br /> <b>Jerome James</b> (nosferatu, carthian)<br /> <b>Sam Bast</b> (nosferatu, carthian)<br /> <br /> Konrad stands before Michael Seville and begins speaking in german. He welcomes Seville into his home and offers him hospitality. Michael Seville thanks him for the offer, but prefers to get down to business.<br /> <br /> In a nearby study, several chairs are arranged. One each for Seville and Konrad are positioned near to each other within comfortable speaking distance. There is a third chair not far from those for Helen. Behind each elder is seating for their respective retinue.<br /> <br /> Konrad explains the situation that we have just discussed an hour ago in the dining room. &quot;This change in the city will bring opportunists. I therefore propose an alliance of mutual defense. A move against our territory is a move against your territory. A move against your territory is a move against our territory.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a long pause before Michael Seville responds.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;How about this: Before, during, and after the transition House Von Berg and House Seville shall remain.&quot;<br /> <b>Konrad:</b> &quot;Agreed.&quot;<br /> <b>Helen:</b> &quot;Witnessed. I saw no transgressions.&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus:</b> &quot;This agreement, is it to be kept secret?&quot;<br /> <b>Seville</b> (switching back to English): &quot;Print brochures if you want.&quot; And with that Helen, Seville and his retinue depart.<br /> <br /> I wasn't 100% sure as to what terms the two Elders had agreed. So, I had a brief conversation with my uncle Quintus who explained it to me. Basically, Von Berg and Seville have agreed to come to one another's defense in the face of existential threats. Seville will not intervene because a rival vampire has made a move on one of our territories. However, if there is a conflict which escalates to all out war we would be obligated to come to one another's aid.<br /> <br /> Before Alice and I left, we had a brief conversation with my Grand Sire. There were two points he wished to impress upon Alice and me.<br /> <br /> 1: &quot;Your territory is the most likely place where our adversaries will test our resolve. Be vigilant. Do not allow them to take what is ours.&quot;<br /> 2: &quot;Antoni is stubborn and proud. Watch his back. Help him even if he does not ask for it.&quot; (Antoni's territory is adjacent to ours and he is the city's Reeve.)<br /> <br /> Also, this move puts an end to Uncle Septimus' Princely ambitions. His strategy depended heavily on convincing Octavia to swear her fealty to him, and with the combined might of his organization and hers plus his alliance with Pilgrim (gangrel priscus, archbishop) and presumably the rest of the family and their pull with the Ordo Dracul would form the coalition needed to push him onto the throne and keep him there. However, it is unlikely the rest of Invictus would fall in line now that Octavia has left the covenant. &quot;You can't even keep your own family in line. How can you expect to keep the whole city together?&quot;<br /> <br /> Another consequence of this move is that Felicity, who had been having trouble choosing between Invictus and Ordo Dracul will now almost certainly join the Order. Felicity had told me that Octavia and I were her two main role models and she was trying to decide which path to follow between Dragon and Invictus.<br /> <br /> When the game began the family was about 7 invictus to 4 dragons. This will make it 7 dragons to 6 invictus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Tears</u></b><br /> Alice and I take the rest of our coterie (Susan Small and Christina) to Susan's house to talk. Susan lives in the guest house of Konrad Von Berg, so it is a short trip. Christina is very upset to hear her mommy has switched covenants.<br /> <br /> <b>Christina:</b> &quot;I'm so alone. Everyone in my Coterie is a Dragon and now my Sire is leaving Invictus!&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;What about your brother Antony? I doubt he will be switching sides any time soon.&quot;<br /> <b>Christina: </b>&quot;He doesn't count! He's adopted! And besides, he has a stick so far up his ass, he doesn't even know the meaning of the word fun.&quot; *sob*<br /> <br /> We try our best to console Christina, who is about to become a very wealthy vampire. Octavia's lands and fortunes will be divided amongst Invictus members of the household. As Octavia's heir, I suspect Christina will be getting a better than even share.<br /> <br /> After the crying is over we agree that we need to do our best to aid Octavia during her time of transition. This mission will start in Elysium, where we will keep our ears open for opposing propaganda whilst catapulting forth our own. This is mostly Christina's and Susan's responsibility. They are harpies, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Empty Nest</u></b><br /> <br /> A few chapters ago, Alice and I captured Aika and Aiko (daeva twins, lancea sanctum.) We won their freedom in court, threw them into human sized birdcages in our basement (what? who doesn't have birdcages in their basement?) We blood bound them and did terrible things to their minds using a custom Dominate devotion I call &quot;the Stepford Devotion.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I have wanted to make them follow Alice and me around to help keep us safer as we execute the duties of Marshal. Who am I kidding? I want us to look cool when we enter rooms flanked by kickass twin vampires.<br /> <br /> Well, we have not seen the twins in several days. I have assumed up to this point that they joining Felicity's diners club in the kiddie pool. I ordered them to do so when Elliot Jr. was in town, and I haven't told them to stop. So, Alice and I visit the speakeasy which we helped to build and is now being run by Felicity and her coterie.<br /> <br /> Felicity confirms that Aika and Aiko have continued to join her for diner's club, but she doesn't know where they go after. Next, we travel north to the territory where the twins made their haven prior to their new legal status. No luck. Well, perhaps there is trouble. So, we travel to Elysium in search of Alice's grandsire Peter (seneschal.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Wiretap</u></b><br /> <br /> We arrive at Elysium and Alice climbs the stairs to the floor where several higher status vampires are given offices. She finds Peter and tells him about the lost twins. Peter tells her that the twins are being used by the city on a mission of some kind. They will be returned to us soon enough. Not to worry. Well, that's a relief.<br /> <br /> So, as we are walking back down the stairs we are approached by Caroline Key. Longtime readers might remember that Caroline was sired without permission and blood bound to her Sire, Fitzgerald in New York. The two fled the authorities and arrived in the kiddie pool at the same time Alice and I did. Entirely to satisfy my own Envy, I arranged to steal Caroline from Fitzgerald and see him to his final death. Later, during a night of Indulgence I tricked Caroline into signing herself over to me as a slave in exchange for safety. Since then, I have sold the girl to the Master of Elysium (Madeline Ross) in exchange for the right to open an official Elysium which will be run by Christina. Sorry for the rambling. The game has been running for a long time.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Caroline Key asks us to join her in the office of Madeline Ross. There, Madame Ross asks us to have a look at one of her ghouls. Alice and I use our wondertwin (i mean wonderspouse) powers and discover the following.<br /> <br /> 1. This ghoul has been dominated by (I assume) a rogue ventrue.<br /> 2. The ghoul, who is an attendant who works at Elysium overhear Michael Seville's travel plans and destination for the evening.<br /> 3. She passed that information along to a ghoul attendant belonging to Hope (QZ resident.)<br /> <br /> We look and see that Madeline Ross is having a conversation with Michael Seville. It is obvious that Seville wants to leave, but Madame Ross is a skilled conversationalist. She is making it really hard for him to leave the conversation before she has finished explaining the finer points of some aspect of art history while remaining polite.<br /> <br /> Well, we get her attention and that of Seville and let them know what we know. Madame Ross further explains that they became aware of the situation because all outbound calls from Elysium are monitored. Apparently the ghoul attendant of Hope picked up the phone and called her to let her know when and where Seville would be this night.<br /> <br /> Seville lets Madame Ross know that he in no way blames her for what has happened, and then excuses himself.<br /> <br /> So, it looks like we have a security breech on our hands, and a likely assassination attempt on Michael Seville in progress.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Anti-Climax</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I head down the lower level parking garage. There, we see a van being filled with fighter type kindred. Luis (mekhet, dragon) invites to climb aboard. Alice and declines, saying we have our own ride. In the car, Alice tells me the reason she wanted to drive separate is that in times such as this, the chain of command would go to the senior Mekhet. Luis is a little older than Alice and Alice is not in the mood to follow orders.<br /> <br /> We travel to the QZ, which is where Seville was planning to be that night. We travel under cloak of Obfuscate looking for trouble, but we can't find any. All the kindred residents of the QZ seem to be up to their normal activities. After a long night of searching for trouble, we check in with out superiors and go home.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Small Claims Court</u></b><br /> <br /> The next night Alice and I are expected to provide security at Antony's bar for some kind of dispute resolution. When we arrive there, we can see that several kindred from both the Quarantine Zone and Kiddie Pool are walking in. Among them is a vampire I have never seen before.<br /> <br /> I approach her, identify myself, and ask who she is and what she is doing here. She tells me that she is from Montreal where her sire was diablerized. She has tracked the diablerist to this city and she will have justice. Johnathan Poole diablerized her sire and he will not escape her.<br /> <br /> Johnathan Poole (daeva, carthian, white night to women everywhere) arrived in the QZ several months ago, but is not a diablerist. During his initial mekhet screening it was discovered that he left Montreal because someone started a rumor that he was a diablerist or had helped one or something like that. Anyway, we are quite sure that Johnathan isn't the vampire she is looking for.<br /> <br /> Well, I know that if she walks into that gathering and starts pointing fingers it isn't going to turn out well. So, I do what comes natural: I hit her with Dominate and escort her to my basement, where I lock her up in a bird cage. I'm a busy man, she'll have to wait till I'm free to settle her problem for her. And because I'm not a monster, I leave her a radio and some books to read.<br /> <br /> It's a good thing that Antony's bar is not far from our Haven. We are able to arrive in time for the proceedings to start. In the hallway, Abigail Taft is rabble rousing a little more than usual. Alice and I pass her by and head in.<br /> <br /> Sharon Winter (gangrel, invictus, sire of Kade) is presiding today. There are some minor cases heard. One case involves a rare book which is owned by a coterie of three. The book is loaned out in exchange for a boon. 1 book. 1 boon. 3 vampires. Who gets the boon?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Death of the Prince</u></b><br /> <br /> What had been intended to be a court for minor dispute resolution now has one serious case to try. Hope, the vampire whose ghoul attendant made the phone call to let her know where Seville was planning to be later that night is on trial. However, before the trial can begin the doors to the bar burst open and in comes Getter.<br /> <br /> <b>Getter:</b> &quot;It's happened! It's finally happened!! The Prince is dead!!!&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;You shut your whore mouth!&quot; *STAB*<br /> <br /> I couldn't help it. I was really angry. Sharon clears her throat.<br /> <br /> <b>Sharon Winter:</b> &quot;Yes, yes. The Prince is dead. Long live the Prince. Court is still in session. Order please.&quot;<br /> <br /> This took the wind right out of my sails and I let Getter limp away.<br /> <br /> <b>Hope:</b> &quot;Does this mean I get to go? The Prince is dead so....&quot;<br /> <b>Sharon:</b> &quot;Of course not, your trial will continue.&quot;<br /> <b>Hope:</b> &quot;This is bullshit! Let me go!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hope is restrained and Alice and I follow Getter out of the bar, where Abigail Taft is make a speech to the assembled kindred. She is telling them that they need to create an interim government as soon as possible so as to prevent chaos. To that end, there will be a meeting at the Drum Club to discuss it more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The First Thing We Do, Let's Kill All the Lawyers</u></b><br /> <br /> The Drum Club is owned by Dorris Bettes. It is located in the northern part of Seville's territory (all carthian territory is Seville's territory.) Alice and I make our way (obfuscate) there to listen in and take names of those who will have to be punished. Abigail begins by explaining the situation.<br /> <br /> <b>Abigail:</b> &quot;Last night while the security apparatus of the city was distracted by a false lead, the prince was slain by his own slaves.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice assures me that the Prince cannot be dead. She is His great grandchilde. She would have felt something.<br /> <br /> So, the meeting continues with Abigail saying that they should have Carthian Prince. Or maybe they shouldn't have a Prince at all. But whatever they do have, it should be Carthian led. Soon, people are calling for Michael Seville to be present. Seville arrives and people begin to bombard him with questions and encourage him to take control of the city.<br /> <br /> <b>the crowd:</b> &quot;We need a Carthian Prince!&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;What makes you think you don't have one already?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a weird comment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Debriefing and a Little Out of Character Information</u></b><br /> <br /> When we arrived back at our haven, Aika and Aiko were waiting for us. We asked them where they had been and what they were up to? The explained to us that they had been scooped up by the seneschal and sent on a mission to expose the disloyal in the city.<br /> <br /> Out of character, the ST occasionally grants special awards instead of XP. over the course of the this game Alice and I have each been awarded 1 Fate Point each. They can be used to change the way the world works in ways both large and small. We had been saving them but finally decided to spend them.<br /> <br /> For me, I spent my fate point to ensure that when I used 'the Stepford Devotion' on the twins, the results would be perfect. So, no rolls were required. It just worked. The personalities of Aika and Aiko have been changed on a fundamental level, and their loyalty to House Fox is assured.<br /> <br /> So, the Seneschal looked into the brains and Aika and Aiko and decided that it was safe to use them as double agents.<br /> <br /> Alice was a little more ambitious with the expenditure of her point. You see, Konrad had been trying to convince Octavia to join the Order for decades with no success. She just wasn't going to budge. But with the use of a Fate Point, Alice and I were able to tip Octavia over the edge and convince her to change the course of her unlife.<br /> <br /> Alice and I as players thought it would be fun to help Octavia pick up the pieces and regain her status in the city. Alice and I as characters wanted to ensure that House Von Berg would maintain hegemony within the Baltimore Ordo Dracul now and in the future of Konrad's eventual torpor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Book Keeping</u></b><br /> <br /> A few notes:<br /> <br /> 1. We did release the newcomer looking to avenge her Sire from the bird cage. She was a member of Invictus. She would not take Alice's and my word for it that Johnathan Poole had been vetted. So, we arranged a meeting between her and Antony (invictus.) She did believe him. We arranged transportation out of town for her and sent her on her way. And yes, of course Alice and I did out Auspex/Dominate tag team interrogation to make sure she wasn't part of something more nefarious.<br /> <br /> 2. The Golden Fleece was handed over to Helen, who I presume handed it over to Pedro. We did not mention the name of the thief as we have not yet finished our full investigation. We've been busy.<br /> <br /> 3. There are a few more orphaned ghouls in the QZ, including Blood. We rounded them up and had a ghoul pageant at the Jiffy Lube. The event included a talent show and a swimsuit competition. Of the orphaned ghouls, two were adopted. Blood was one of them. The rest were creamated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Finish What You Started</u></b><br /> <br /> Soon after, we were approached by Peter (seneschal) in his official capacity. He was flanked by a few members of the mekhetocracy and bearing a writ of destruction.<br /> <br /> Peter: &quot;Why don't you go finish what you started.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Death Warrant bears the name of Getter, who is to be executed for the crime of not showing sufficient grief when the Prince (fake) died. Before we went looking for Getter, we went looking for Snow. We remembered our agreement with Shaman. And in all honesty, I am happy to hand her over to him. I much prefer to see orphaned ghouls adopted rather than have to go to the trouble of having to kill them and cover it up.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Snow is the second girl to end up in one of the bird cages in my basement this game session. She is provided with books, radio, tv, food, and a portable toilet. We are humane jailors. Getter proved neither hard to find nor to kill.<br /> <br /> We informed Shaman that his adoption was about to go through.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;Can you use your powers to make the transition a little more... smooth?&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;That costs extra.&quot;<br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;Fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Reward</u></b><br /> <br /> The game session ended with one last visitor to our haven. It is Peter, Alice's grandsire. The Seneschal/herald has arrived to thank me for the hard work I have been putting into the QZ. He hands me an indulgence granting permission to sure a new vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Peter:</b> &quot;Keep up the good work.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know why Peter rewarded me and not Alice in this way. But I do know that Peter is of the opinion that the newcomers should be destroyed whenever possible. Every one of them who earns Baltimore Citizenship takes a spot that could be occupied by childer born of Baltimore. Peter is very much a nativist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 09-02-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T06:55:09-07:00","id":648897,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the long silence. Scheduling has been difficult. Finding the time to write has been more difficult. Anyway, thanks for reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: I updated the character portraits for clans <a href=\"http://s12.postimg.org/sz4r4nfp9/Clan_Daeva.png\" target=\"_blank\">Daeva</a>, <a href=\"http://s11.postimg.org/gko4k0rmr/Clan_Gangrel.png\" target=\"_blank\">Gangrel</a>, and <a href=\"http://s17.postimg.org/xychdav2n/Clan_Mekhet.png\" target=\"_blank\">Mekhet</a> to include a few new citizens. Click the link in my signature to check them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 09-02-2015, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T04:59:14-07:00","id":649958,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Way Forward</u></b><br /> <br /> I am told by the ST that Alice and I will soon be rotated out of the front lines for a time and given an opportunity to develop our land and knock antlers with some of the other neonates of the city. We have done what we can to screen the newcomers for rabies and now it's time to see which ones prove themselves worthy of Baltimore Citizenship and which ones will be destroyed.<br /> <br /> To kick off the session, we received a request for a meeting with the Master of Elysium and Antony (reeve.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Site Survey</u></b><br /> <br /> Before our meeting, Alice and I take advantage of this time of relative calm to survey our territory and take stock of our House. Our territory runs along the shore of the Chesapeake Bay. It is bordered by the territory of my Cousin Antony (reeve), the territory of the Coterie of my cousin Darren (censor), and the Territory of Dorris Bettes (daeva, carthian.) The territory itself boasts three main locations of interest:<br /> <br /> 1. There are some industrial docks that have fallen into disrepair. The boat slips need dredging and cranes need maintenance, but the docks could be made serviceable again. This is relevant because Kade (gangrel, dragon, Alice's apprentice in coils) wants to get involved in organized crime. If we were able to get this operation running and hand it off to Kade (and his girlfriend Lorraine Reddington) we might create for ourselves some passive income.<br /> <br /> 2. Close to the new metro station which links this neighborhood to the rest of the city construction is almost finished on a new nightclub. The club was the dream of Kat (gangrel, carthian) who came to Baltimore because it has a reputation for having a thriving cosplay community. So, we made a deal with Kat: We would go in 50/50 on the construction costs of the venue and when it is open, she will run it. It will hopefully become good feeding ground in the near future.<br /> <br /> 3. Christina has also been working on a building project. You may recall that we have bargained to get permission from Madeline Ross (master of Elysium) to open an official Elysium of our own. Sure, there are other kindred meeting places in the city but none of them have the official status of Elysium. Ours will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Trouble in Paradise?</u></b><br /> <br /> One thing we notice while familiarizing ourselves with our new domain is that construction is not proceeding very quickly on Christina's future Elysium venue. There are other sites around locust point where crews are working twenty-four hours a day under the glare of high powered work lights. Not so at Christina's place. So we made plans to speak to Antony after our meeting with the Keeper. You see, one of Antoni's main mortal influences is that he owns more than one construction firm and has influence with several others. If you want something build quickly and discreetly, Antony is your man. We figured he could smooth things out for us.<br /> <br /> The meeting takes place in Antony's bar. When we arrive there, we see that Antony has pulled out a dining table into the bar with place settings for 12. The settings have fine silverware and doilies and whatnot. I wonder if this is meant to be a formal affair. Fortunately it turned out not to be, but Antony was covering his bases. Anyway, Madeline Ross arrives and drops a bombshell on us.<br /> <br /> Madeline Ross: &quot;The Prince has ordered me to shut down Elysium and rebuild it at a new venue. As such, your Elysium will be the only Elysium for some time. Please do hurry in completing its construction. I do not want there to be a loss of continuity of service during the transition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Holy shit, this is a big opportunity for our Coterie to show the city we are cool for reasons other than violence. However, before Madame Ross leaves she asks Antony to use his construction connections to speed the progress on her project. Fuck. Now we can't ask him. Gotta figure something out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>At Octavia's House</u></b><br /> <br /> We hadn't had much time to speak to our Liege Lord since the family dinner as were busy babysitting the newcomers in the QZ. When we arrived at Octavia's estate, she was not home. We sat in her library and waited for a few hours for her return. Konrad Von Berg has become her mentor in the Ordo Dracul and she is therefore spending a lot of time with him. I'm not really comfortable with calling Octavia a 'slave' so I hope she learns some coils soon.<br /> <br /> Note from the ST: &quot;Octavia is a lot older than a neonate. It will be a lot more difficult for her to change herself. Also, she doesn't have a lot of XP to spend right now. So don't expect a meteoric rise within the Order.&quot; Fine...<br /> <br /> Anyway, we did finally get to speak with Octavia and inquire as to her plans.<br /> <br /> <b>Octavia:</b> &quot;Right now, I am watching and waiting. But soon, I am going to make a lot of kindred very uncomfortable. I have been stripped of my lands and titles as a result of my choice to join the Order. That doesn't change the fact that I am very ambitious and very capable. I will soon make a move on someone's territory and take it for my own. I was once a regent of the City and I will be again.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are two territories that Octavia has her eyes on now:<br /> <br /> 1. The territory of Sharon Winter (gangrel, ancilla, invictus, Kade's sire) is located on the eastern border of the University (dragon territory.) Sharon has sworn her fealty to Octavia. However, Octavia's change of Covenant will give Sharon an opportunity to have her agreement voided. If Sharon keeps faith with Octavia, Octavia will keep faith with Sharon. However, if Sharon does decide to leave Octavia's service, Octavia will attack Sharon's influence and holdings with the goal of leaving her landless.<br /> <br /> 2. Bellinsky makes his territory in Little Italy. Little Italy has changed hands a few times over the course of the game. It was initially Lancea Sanctum territory, but Pilgrim gifted it to Bellinsky (invictus) and Elliot Rex (carthian); the brothers nosferatu. The brothers divided the territory, each taking half for themself. Since the death of Elliot Rex I have wondered if his half of Little Italy would be inherited by his brother Bellinsky or if as a Carthian his territory would pass into the hands of the carthians and thus Michael Seville. In either case, if Sharon Winter keeps her agreement with Octavia this is where Octavia will strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Octavia:</b> &quot;And besides, you already have a perfectly legitimate casus belli with Bellinsky. He has been interfering with construction in your territory.&quot;<br /> <br /> AHA! Wait, what? It's Bellinsky? I kind of assumed it was Dorris Bettes. Time will tell.<br /> <br /> <br /> This should bring the story up to date. There might or might not be a session this weekend. Nevertheless, my interest in this game continues to be high. All credit to my ST who is really the best in the business. Thanks for reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 09-03-2015, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:52:06-07:00","id":650304,"title":"","content":"Thank you for writting! Curious and curiouser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T11:24:51-07:00","id":650330,"title":"","content":"So nice to have you back, figurehead!<br /> <br /> I'm curious about one thing: Does that sentence you mentioned in the last 7th chapter post (&quot;I am told by the ST that Alice and I will soon be rotated out of the front lines for a time and given an opportunity to develop our land and knock antlers with some of the other neonates of the city.&quot;) and the recent events mean that the whole &quot;deadly external foes&quot; and the Prince situation will be left more into the background and less into your hands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T02:54:49-07:00","id":650999,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; I don't know why Peter rewarded me and not Alice in this way. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Felix is married to Alice. What's his is hers and what's hers is his. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T09:45:48-07:00","id":651392,"title":"","content":"Hey thanks guys. It's good to be back <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Phersus: The external deadly threats are still very much a part of the story, but they are operating on a vampire time scale. Behind the scenes, parties from outside the city have been probing Baltimore trying to find out whether or not the Prince has succumbed to torpor yet. In this setting, the Prince of Baltimore is a seriously powerful Elder. He is feared far and wide. Those who look to Baltimore with avarice would probably prefer to wait until he is off the board before invading. There have been a few scenes in which the Prince has acted to remind outsiders that he is still very much active.<br /> <br /> 1. There was the night that a nosferatu elder from New York visited midnight mass. I don't know if it was a coincidence that that night was a night of indulgence, but the Prince assembled all the mekhet (and one ventrue) and together we destroyed that vampire.<br /> <br /> 2. Then there was the night the Prince asked us all to assemble and be ready to fight he gave a small speech/warning to a vampire who he then killed. If I am not mistaken, that vampire was merely a pawn who was being possessed by the Prince of Philadelphia.<br /> <br /> So, there have been reminders sent to the nearest domains that Baltimore is still very much under the protection and control of the Prince. Also, the ST has been hinting that Philadelphia have been corrupted by Belial's Brood. I suspect that one way or another we will see a conflict with Philadelphia that will end in violence, and Alice and I will be there.<br /> <br /> <br /> @tsusasi: So true, and she's not shy about it. Regardless, Konrad has made it clear that the next Ventrue who will allowed to sire will be Octavia. So, even if I were inclined to sire at this time I would have to get in line. As for Alice, I don't think she is interested in becoming a mommy yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, I took a few minuets to create a chart of the Ordo Dracul roster with master/apprentice relationships shown. [<a href=\"http://s24.postimg.org/8uhpnlwx1/Ordo_Dracul.png\" target=\"_blank\">LINK</a>]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:40:59-07:00","id":652933,"title":"","content":"Thank your for the answer. You know, figurehead... i'm dying to know how Felix and Alice would react to the Stryx. It will be (as it was) funny seeing the clash with Belial's Brood and of course other ancillae (we can take Felix and Alice in that power level, right?). But against the Owls... :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:41:20-07:00","id":659404,"title":"","content":"Some really interesting things happened during our last play session. I'll have to wait and see what comes of the developments before I write about them though. In the mean time, I created a chart of all the non-citizen vampires in the area to help me better understand what's going on. Hopefully it'll tide you over a bit. [<a href=\"http://s30.postimg.org/6asvx0v6n/non_citizens.png\" target=\"_blank\">non-citizen vampire chart</a>.]<br /> <br /> As for the strix, we will never know. Thankfully all members of our group are in agreement: the strix were a terrible idea and a terrible waste of pages in the new edition. Let's not discuss it any further in this thread though please.<br /> <br /> Edit: Updated the chart to include vampires from all the territories surrounding Baltimore. Note that some characters' covenants are written with an upper case first letter and others with lower case. This is an indication of whether or not they have fully committed to their choice and/or have been fully accepted by the covenant. Known coteries are grouped in blue boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 09-10-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:51:47-07:00","id":659414,"title":"","content":"Daeva - Canadian Johnathon Poole Is a Canadian invasion one of the latest developments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:07:08-07:00","id":659421,"title":"","content":"lol no. He's a carthian, but he did emigrate from Montreal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:45:13-07:00","id":659807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/648872-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-8?p=659404#post659404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the strix, we will never know. Thankfully all members of our group are in agreement: the strix were a terrible idea and a terrible waste of pages in the new edition. Let's not discuss it any further in this thread though please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Well, i personally enjoy them a lot, but i know others don't share my point of view. Fair enough. Keep the adventures coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T09:00:03-07:00","id":674285,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Security Measures</u></b><br /> <br /> I forgot to mention two topics that came up when Antony, Alice, and I were talking to Madeline Ross (daeva, master of Elysium) at Antony's bar: Due to the recent breach of security at the city Elysium, two policy changes have taken effect.<br /> <br /> 1. Until recently, the Elysium was open to any who could find it. This included newcomers to the city and their ghouls. Due to the recent security breech, this default state of welcome has been rescinded.<br /> <br /> 2. Certain influential kindred in the city (read: invictus) will no longer accept letters unless they are written on watermarked paper and sealed with wax. The watermarks and wax seal should be unique to the kindred sending the letter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Sherrie &amp; Fishie</u></b><br /> <br /> Over the course of the game, there have been several vampires who have done us wrong. The ones that have pissed me off the most were the ones that have targeted our haven, our family, or both. So far, we have prevailed against our enemies, and we have tried to do so in a way that sends a message to others who would consider similar actions. Such messages have come in the form of public duels and in one case the destruction of an entire bloodline.<br /> <br /> And then there is the case of Fishie. Fishie, formally known as Sharol rebelled against her daeva sister Catherine and was expelled from the territory of Roy. She wound up working for Pasha in the now fallow NE side. In the course of her duties, she attempted to kidnap Felicity (my vampire sister) twice, and she has been paying for her crime ever since.<br /> <br /> Alice and I decided to ruin her and release her into the Quarantine Zone. We beat her down again and again. We took steps to make sure that no coterie would ever accept her. Even the notoriously Canadian white knight Jonathan Poole gave up on her. Occasionally, a flicker of conscience will enter my thoughts and I remind myself that her employers intended to sacrifice Felicity in some kind of Blood Sorcery ritual.<br /> <br /> In part 6 of the write up, I mentioned that after the &quot;Dark Lord&quot; and his progeny were destroyed we decided to take a prisoner. Sherry (daeva, unaligned) has been staying in one of the rooms of our haven for a while now. Both of Sherry's vampire siblings were blood bound to their sire. Somehow, Sherry managed to avoid that fate and convince her sire that she was in fact bound to him. We took it as evidence that she had a better head on her shoulders than her compatriots and offered her a deal: &quot;Come with us and do what we say and you will live. Don't, and die the final death.&quot;<br /> <br /> Our intention is this: We will groom this girl for Baltimore Citizenship and membership in the Circle of the Crone. It is our hope that we can gift her to Appolonia (daeva priscus) in an effort to make up for the fact that we have taken two members of her clan as our slaves (Aika and Aiko.) This is a long term project obviously.<br /> <br /> Before we could begin training the girl there were some hurdles for us to leap:<br /> <br /> 1. I wasn't going to proceed with this plan if the only thing keeping her in line is fear of death or worse. When we brought her to our place, she was convinced that we were planning to turn her into a sex slave or something. It took several conversations to convince her that were not going to do that. We also had to shine a light on her previous situation (that she was spawned from a bloodline whose patriarch actually called himself 'the dark lord' with a straight face.) and convinced her that she is being given a gift in the form of an opportunity to be something other than sex slave/cannon fodder in the 'dark lord's army.<br /> <br /> 2. In exchange for a boon, the notary created for us an Invictus contract solidifying our teacher student relationship. We also, made sure that Kade's girlfriend Lorraine met the girl. Lorraine knows Majesty, and in the event that Sherry tries to run away, Lorraine can call her back.<br /> <br /> 3. We invited Melissa Hopps (daeva, harpy, groom, circle) to join us at our haven one night. When she arrived, I introduced her to Sherry and asked her for some advice. When Melissa saw that there was *another* daeva under our roof she giggled.<br /> <br /> <b>Melissa:</b> &quot;Felix, do you have thing for daeva?&quot;<br /> <br /> Once she was done teasing me, she was willing to offer a little advice. She told me that I should be careful because of the relationship between Appolonia and her childe Calypso (daeva, crone, ancilla.) Calypso does not want to learn cruac. In our game, blood sorcery and standard disciplines are mutually exclusive. So, if Calypso were to begin learning cruac, she would lose access to decades of experience with other disciplines.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if a new daeva were to join the Circle and embrace cruac, they may one day eclipse Calypso's position in the circle and perhaps in her mother's heart. Melissa advised us that if we were able, we should mold the girl such that she would accept the philosophy of the Crone, and train her to be competent in her chosen occupation. She warned us that if we do too good a job, we could make an enemy of Calypso. We shall have to walk a fine line, but in the end we owe a debt to Apollonia. Not her daughter.<br /> <br /> So, since Alice and I have been rotated out of the Quarantine Zone we have more free time on our hands. I decided that it was time to start training Sherry. But first, I wanted to make it clear how high the stakes were for her. Well, I have a little while back learned the fifth dot of Obfuscate (cloak the gathering, not the 2nd ed holodeck power.) So I took her invisibly across the bay so she could see what life was like for Fishie.<br /> <br /> We arrived at the 'Private Eye' which is a strip club where Fishie works a few nights a week. After she finished her shift there, we followed her back onto the street. Fishie wandered around for awhile until she found Shaman (nosferatu, carthian.)<br /> <br /> <b>Fishie:</b> &quot;Can I have a ticket?&quot;<br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;You still haven't paid me for the last one.&quot;<br /> <b>Fishie:</b> &quot;You know I'm good for it.&quot;<br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;You owe me.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the Quarantine Zone, newcomers have two options when it comes to legal feeding:<br /> 1. They can drink cold blood from the butcher shop. The almoner (Cooper) provides this blood as part of his official capacity as a city official. However, drinking here is a catch 22<br /> a. Cooper is required to provide enough blood to keep the beast at bay to anyone who asks. However, taking your meals here is an admission that you are not able to feed yourself. You will lose face.<br /> b. Any blood provided over and above what is needed to keep the beast at bay, and you owe Cooper a boon.<br /> 2. Your other option comes in the form of tickets. They are distributed in limited numbers and the color changes from month to month so as to prevent overfeeding.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Shaman is something of a loan shark where the tickets are concerned. So, with a ticket in her pocket Fishie turns and heads north along the main road in the QZ. Eventually she finds a john and pulls him into an alley. Money changes hands and Fishie drops to her knees. In the course performing fellatio, Fishie sinks her fangs into her john. She leaves with a little cash, a little blood, and a very satisfied customer. As she leaves she pulls the ticket out of her pocket, tears it in two, and drops it on the street.<br /> <br /> Sherry wants to know why we have made her watch this. &quot;Because there are fates worse than death.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Broom</u></b><br /> <br /> One fine evening, Alice and I are summoned in our official capacity as Marshals. We are to accompany Seville, Spider (nosferatu), and Jerome James (nosferatu) into the Quarantine Zone. Most of the newcomers have arrived from Council Territory, which is slowly but surely being abandoned by vampires.<br /> <br /> There is one newcomer who is from farther afield. The vampire in question is named Broom, and he is nosferatu. There have been rumors of a powerful nosferatu in the area, and Seville has decided to look into the matter personally. So, the group of us arrive near the Jiffy-Lube where the area's vampires hang out. We ask one of the newcomers where we can find Broom, but he is not keen on telling us where he is.<br /> <br /> <b>Jerome James:</b> &quot;If you do not take us to Broom, you will regret it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice, Jerome, Spider, and I are led to Broom. Seville is invisible and presumably following us. Our journey is not long, as Broom is hanging out in the parking lot behind the Jiffy-Lube talking to a few other vampires. There is definitely a feeling of power in the air. I am not sure if we are detecting blood potency, nightmare aura, or a little of both.<br /> <br /> Seville emerges from the shadows and introduces himself to Broom. There is a little small talk in which Broom reveals that he is from New York before Seville gets down to business.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;I hear we may have a new priscus in town.&quot;<br /> <b>Broom:</b> &quot;Oh... You can call me that if you want to.&quot; (false modesty)<br /> <br /> <br /> There is a blur as Seville closes the distance to Broom and grabs him by the throat. They lock eyes for a minute before Broom is frozen in fear. Seville releases him and walks away.<br /> <br /> Back at Seville's office, he tells us that he may have made a mistake by losing his temper that way. Seville turns to Spider and orders him to travel to New York and find out whatever he can about Broom's pedigree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Elysium</u></b><br /> <br /> About a week later, Alice and I went to Elysium. A few things of note occured.<br /> <br /> 1. We were approached by Susan Small (ventrue, dragon, harpy, cousin, coterie-mate.)<br /> <b>Susan:</b> &quot;You didn't hear? Pilgrim has distributed a new batch of golden tickets to the newcomers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ah... the golden tickets. It has been several years since Pilgrim has handed them out. They are very valuable for multiple reasons. First is simple entertainment value. Pilgrim throws good parties. The greater value comes in the form of access. Some elders are easy to get an audience with, like Seville. Pilgrim is on the opposite side of the spectrum. I have only had two conversations with the man in all the years I have been in Baltimore. In fact, it was at the last golden ticket event that Pilgrim revealed to me that I had a sister. So yeah. I want the tickets.<br /> <br /> 2. As we were leaving, Simon (mekhet, ancilla, archon, lance) handed us a sealed envelope.<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;Open it tomorrow when you wake.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Looking for Tickets</u></b><br /> <br /> Well, if the tickets have been disbursed in the QZ, that is where we will go. After asking some questions we learned a few things about this year's batch of tickets.<br /> <br /> 1. Some of the tickets are issued to the bearer, meaning they can be traded and anyone can use them. Others have been issued to specific individuals.<br /> <br /> 2. Dorris Bettes has already made it a point to inform the newbies that the tickets are in fact valuable. I guess I won't be able to swindle the newcomers. That's a bummer. And also, I really dislike Dorris Bettes.<br /> <br /> Another vampire who was upset that Dorris let the cat out of the bag was Shaman. As I have mentioned before he something of a trader. I know he would have liked to get his hands on them cheap and resell them. He did manage to get one though, and he did owe me a boon for our assistance with his ghoul attendant, Snow. So, Shaman gave us his ticket. One down. Four to go.<br /> <br /> Also during our search, we stopped by the Jiffy-Lube made it known that we were looking for tickets, and that anyone interested in selling should speak with us. A newcomer named Mark West approaches us and states that he would trade is his ticket in exchange for advice and assistance in getting permission to blood bond another newcomer named Molly McMillan. He would be willing to accept Piper Morgan or Delores Nelson as alternate choices. We declined.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Abandon all Hope</u></b><br /> <br /> The next evening after Alice and I awoke, we broke the seal on Simon's letter. It read simply: &quot;Empty your house of anyone who is not Felix Fox or Alice Fox.&quot; So, we gathered Sidney, Mouse, Aika, Aiko, Sherri, and all our other staffers and sent them downtown with instructions to hang out at a hotel and not to return until dawn approaches.<br /> <br /> Over the course of about an hour, three groups of kindred arrive.<br /> <br /> 1st: My cousin Antony (ventrue, reeve, invictus) arrives. He is accompanied by a retinue of ghouls. The vampire Hope is with them. She is gagged and in chains. Antony doesn't know why he has been summoned here. He received a letter from Simon just like us.<br /> 2nd: The doorbell rings and Spider (nosferatu) is at our doorstep. We invite him in, and he lingers in the doorway for a few moments before he shuts it at which point Seville appears. We welcome them both into our home and walk into the parlor where hope is kneeling on the floor looking very upset. Apparently, neither Spider nor Seville know why they have been summoned here either. Seville looks at Hope and says: &quot;Oh. Is this entertainment?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville also asks Alice and I to stop by his office tomorrow for tea.<br /> <br /> 3rd: &quot;We hear the garage door opening and sounds of vehicles pulling in. Soon, a small parade comes marching up the stairs. First come Kyle (mekhet) and a ghoul. They pause, holding the door open for an unkown number of invisible kindred. Last to enter are Kyle (a second Kyle) and Betty (Alice's sister.)<br /> <br /> The various guests arrange themselves in our parlor and one of the Kyles removes Hope's gag.<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;Relax. We are here to look into your grievance.&quot;<br /> <b>Hope:</b> &quot;Oh. Yeah, right. I want to see the Prince. I want to report a plot against the Prince. Felix and Alice are plotting against the Prince!&quot;<br /> Kyle stares at Hope for a while.<br /> <b>Hope:</b> &quot;Stop staring at me!&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Kyle turns to Alice and me.<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;These are very serious accusations. Of all the kindred in this room I would suspect Felix the most. Plotting. Travelling between cities. Carrying orders.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice and I each in turn feel a gentle pressure on our minds followed by a breeze as Kyle (obviously the Prince) searches our minds for signs of disloyalty or evidence of a plot against him. Next, there is silence in the room as the various mekhet commune in silence with one another.<br /> <br /> Simon, who arrived under the guise of the first ghoul puts the gag back on Hope's mouth and asks: &quot;Do you have any stakes in this house?&quot;<br /> <br /> Before we can respond, Antony pulls one out of his coat. Always prepared that one. Hope is staked and carried away by Antony, leaving only the 2nd and 3rd groups to arrive remaining. The mekhet in the room begin to trade places and faces with one another in an impressive display of obfuscate/shell game. When they finish, there are still two Kyles. This time, one of them obviously exudes the predatory aura of an elder.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;Be seated.&quot; Then he turns to Seville and says: &quot;I see your agent has returned from New York. Have you any news?&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;I would have made a report if I knew your interest.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville gave us the following information about Broom:<br /> 1. Spider made contact with Lady Montessori (nosferatu, carthian, prince of Brooklyn)<br /> 2. Broom's age is that of an older ancilla, but due to various times spent in torpor his power is that of a mid-level ancilla.<br /> 3. He has fled New York due to blood hunt being called on him by Suzerane (Prince of Manhattan.)<br /> 4. He didn't linger in the outer boroughs for fear that Adhamar (ventrue, Prince of the Bronx, invictus, my grandsire's brother.) Would complete the blood hunt out of courtesy to Suzerane.<br /> 5. He has a reputation for cruelty, ambition, and determination.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;Well, well. You know how to pick your enemies.&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;If you give me permission, I will see to his destruction this night.&quot;<br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;What do you think of him as Prince?&quot;<br /> Seville remains silent.<br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;What about you Felix?&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;No, I don't think he will make a good Prince.&quot;<br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;Why?&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Because you have not named him so.&quot;<br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;How very politic.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;In all seriousness, he is not of our blood. He is not of Baltimore.&quot;<br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;But our enemies will not attack as long as I hold the reigns of power.&quot;<br /> <br /> It never occurred to me that the Prince would really hand the reigns of power to an outsider, and as he continued to speak I could not hold my tongue.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Oh my god, you're going to hand the throne to Septimus.&quot;<br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;No. That would be cruel, but I do think Broom would fit the bill. Perhaps we will fake the death of Michael Seville.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the first time in the game's history Seville lets down his guard and we are able to succeed at an empathy roll against him. He does not like the sounds of this plan.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Kyle</b> Continues: &quot;The city is unassailable as long as I am Prince. Therefore it is better to be attacked while I am Prince.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Let me offer an alternative: We assist Adhamar to take all of New York, then combine our forces to remove the blight from Philadelphia. Adhamar believes Suzerane is completely under the sway of the priests. He has become lethargic.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;Suzerane's throne is built on the bones of those who have thought that. No. Adhamar is a great vampire, and would be a great Prince for another city, but his power is not great enough to take Manhattan.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Kyle:</b> &quot;The Carthian voice will rise. Many will join Broom and he will strike you (Seville) down spectacularly. Publicly. Maintain secrecy of this meeting and prepare for an inhospitable rule. But don't worry. It won't last long.<br /> <br /> After the meeting, Seville is the last to leave. &quot;That offer of tea is still on. See you tomorrow night.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> This covers about half of my notes from the last couple game sessions. More to come when I get a little more time to write. I hope you all enjoy if. Also... wow! We finally know the plan of the Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:31:42-07:00","id":674418,"title":"","content":"Ha! I love the prince of your city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T07:36:55-07:00","id":675224,"title":"","content":"Risky gambit! Having the wisdom and power the Prince seems to have i trust his/her judgement... but there are outsiders as potent as him/her. I'd seriously worry about the power and knowledge of the shadowed enemies. <br /> <br /> Other point i'd wonder about would be about that expression &quot;it won't last long&quot;. Exactly how much time do qualify as &quot;long&quot; for the Prince?<br /> <br /> And last, but certainly not least: won't be suspicious that an Ancilla (and one not that potent as Broom) take the Prince's Mantle uncontestedly? What about all the rest of Baltimore Elders? Will they suffer this boisterous newcomer in silence? This could very well spell civil war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:37:25-07:00","id":691245,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Igloo</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;To the igloo?&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;To the igloo.&quot;<br /> <br /> In Alice's and my second shared haven, we converted a walk-in closet into a normal sized closet hiding a dome shaped concrete bunker. The ceiling was painted with glow in the dark paint to depict the nighttime sky, and there is a comfortable mattress fitted to the space. When we constructed our new residence, we decided to incorporate this kind of sleeping space into the design. This is where we go when we need to discuss things in total privacy. We call it the igloo.<br /> <br /> Inside the igloo, Alice and I lamented the fact that we could not warn the other members of our coterie and family about the coming danger. We resolved to proceed as though everything was normal, and when Broom becomes Prince to oppose his rule, just as we would had we not known the origin of his coming success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Tea With Seville</u></b><br /> <br /> The next night, Alice and I arrive at Seville's office to see he is hosting an open forum with several carthians from the QZ. He asks if anyone has anything they would like to say.<br /> Jonathan Poole rises and talks about modern forms of communication, including telephone, email, and the bulletin boards of the nascent internet. Jonathan thinks these were better, more secure ways to communicate than sending messengers with letters than can be intercepted.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Alice, perhaps you would be willing to help me make a point. Jonathan, call Alice a poopy head.&quot;<br /> <b>Jonathan:</b> &quot;What? I don't want to...&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Do it.&quot;<br /> <b>Jonathan</b>: &quot;Alice... you are a poopy head.&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Now, try it in a letter.&quot;<br /> Jonathan grabs a sheet of scrap paper and begins to write 'Alice, you are a poopy head.'<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;No. That's a note. Write a letter. Try this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Madame Alice Fox, member of the Ordo Dracul, Bailiff to Michael Seville, Marshal to Reeve Antony,<br /> I hope this night finds you well. I have been asked by Alder Michael Seville, priscus of Clan Nosferatu and Carthian Prefect, to call you a 'poopy head.' Please forgive me for this insult. I do not actually think of you in this way.<br /> <br /> I again I hope this letter finds you well.<br /> Sincerely,<br /> Jonathan Poole&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville: &quot;And now if you would all please excuse me, I have an appointment.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville leads Alice and I into his private office, where tea is served as promised. A few topics are discussed:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Alice and I are worried about the meeting we just had with the Prince. Seville assures us that any plans the Prince has laid out will take years to mature. This is at once a relief in that we will have more time to prepare for the worst, and an extended sentence under the sword of Damocles.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;What's this I hear about certain kindred not accepting letters unless they are delivered on pretty stationary?&quot; Last chapter, Madeline Ross told Alice and me that due to the security breech at Elysium, certain kindred would no longer be accepting correspondence unless it arrived on watermarked stationary and sealed with a mark unique to the sender.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot; I was about grab a roll of toilet paper and start a letter writing campaign, but if it's for security...&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Seville:</b> &quot;I have heard the two of you are trying your hands at being a groom.&quot; Seville has a candidate for the embrace and wants Alice and I to prepare him for unlife. &quot;I want you to teach him to think like a vampire. I want you to teach him to think like you think, Alice. I want you to teach him to think like you think, Felix.&quot;<br /> <br /> First, Alice and I are floored. This is a sign of utmost trust. Second... what if we fuck up? We have enjoyed very much being on Seville's good side. We do not want to find our way to his bad side. Seville assures us that if it doesn't work out, he will merely make the guy into a ghoul and there will be no ill will.<br /> <br /> We tell Seville that we will think about it.<br /> <br /> A few days later one of Coopers ghouls arrived at our haven and delivered two letters, addressed to Alice. Both were written by Jonathan Poole. The first followed very closely the format proposed by Michael Seville. The second was a letter of apology for the first.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Information from Sherry</u></b><br /> <br /> Well, to begin preparing for a dark future, I needed information about the latest batch of newcomers from council territory. As it happens, Sherry (daeva, our houseguest) is from council territory. So, I bring her once again across the bridge under the cloak of Obfuscate 5. We find a place to sit on the roof of the storage facility which overlooks the butcher shop and the Jiffy-Lube. I make her write a few notes about each of the vampires we see as they come and go. Here is what she wrote:<br /> <br /> Ghost: Dangerous. Bad. Not too powerful.<br /> Molly McMillan: Sam Wagner wants to drink her tears.<br /> Patrick: Sired in Baltimore. Sire is dead. Sire was in coterie with Mortimer.<br /> Sam Wagner: Wants to blood bond a bunch of vampires.<br /> Shaman: Wizard/Banker/Pawn Shop/Drug Dealer/Werewolf Negotiator<br /> Mark West: Gun Ho Revolutionary. Down with the System.<br /> Vadic Imamu: Wizard/Blood Magic. Goat Sacrifices.<br /> Trenton: Weasel. Opportunist.<br /> Piper Morgan: Feminist.<br /> Karma: Not happy about the treatment of blacks in Baltimore.<br /> Sunny: Involved in some kind of conspiracy.<br /> Marco and Polo: Smarter than they look. Deadlier than they look. Marco once killed a werewolf with his bare hands.<br /> Nick: Member of the Council. Snake? Poison? Wise? Enemy of my (Sherry's) sire.<br /> <br /> These notes aren't nessecarily accurate or in depth, but Sherry was sired in council territory. She knows more about these vampires than I do. After we returned to my haven, the notes were given to Sidney to burn. Yes, I am paranoid. Thanks for asking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ghouls</u></b><br /> <br /> Within our household there are 5 ghouls. One belongs to Alice, and the rest belong to me:<br /> <br /> 1. Sidney: Sidney is the first ghoul either of us ever created. Over time I have raised her to a 5 point retainer. Her main duties are to maintain our security both at home and when we are out and about. Though she is a competent fighter, I value her more for her good judgment. She often has the unenviable duty of keeping Mouse out of trouble.<br /> <br /> 2. Mouse: Mouse is Alice's ghoul. She is insatiably curious and very easy to overlook. These traits can get her into trouble. However, it also makes her a good little spy. We have often sent her on daytime recon missions.<br /> <br /> 3&amp;4. Steve and Eddie: The dayshift. Unlike Sidney and Mouse, Steve and Eddie are not considered attendants. They are not permitted to accompany us to Elysium or to other vampire's havens. They are kept in the dark about the truth of many things. They are the armed guards that patrol the house while Alice and I sleep.<br /> <br /> 5. Banjo the Wonderdog: Banjo is our most recently created ghoul. He is a border collie whom I have trained (animalism 1) to work alongside Sidney. Banjo should not be confused with an attack dog. Sure, he's a dog with a bit of resilience and he can bite and stuff, but his primary duty is to identify threats so Sidney can do her job better.<br /> <br /> Believe it or not, the various ghouls of the city have lives of their own that they pursue when they are not fulfilling their duties to their undead masters. In particular those labeled attendants are permitted to be present at Elysium and other social venues. A while ago we gave Mouse and Sidney permission to participate in the reindeer games when their schedules permit.<br /> <br /> So anyway, one night Mouse says to Alice: &quot;Pascal is making a porno.&quot; ... and Alice sent her to investigate. Really? Well... whatever. Sometimes Mouse needs something to keep her busy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Piper's Problem</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I returned to the QZ in search of more tickets. After a short stroll we find three vampires sitting at a picnic table near the water:<br /> <br /> Shaman (nosferatu, Carthian)<br /> Trenton (daeva, carthian)<br /> Piper Morgan (daeva, Carthian)<br /> <br /> <b>Shaman:</b> &quot;Maybe you should tell Felix about your problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> Piper was reluctant to do so, and I wasn't particularly interested in talking with Trenton present. We sent him away and then Piper slid a piece of paper across the table. It read: &quot;Petitio tua negatur.&quot; (your request is denied.) Piper knew what the paper said, she had Patrick translate it. She told me that she had made a request to the reeve for permission to create a ghoul. She wanted me to smooth it over for her. Piper said she didn't have a ghoul and she needed one Well, Alice and I had committed to not abusing our position as marshals for personal gain. We felt that would show a lack of integrity. However, I did tell Piper that I would ask the Reeve why her request was denied. So, Alice and I paid a visit to Antony (ventrue, invictus, reeve, my cousin (adopted))<br /> <br /> 1. Antony informed us that Piper already had a ghoul. &quot;His name is Charlie and he is one of those goth kids.&quot; Furthermore, there were several vampires in the QZ who didn't have even one. &quot;It would be unfair to give Piper two when others have none.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. I was a little pissed that Piper led me to believe she did not have a ghoul already and make me look stupid in front of the reeve. We went to confront Piper and after a little cajoling she told us that her ghoul, Charlie had recently killed himself. &quot;He killed himself in the bathroom and left me a stupid note!&quot; Piper had already destroyed the note.<br /> <br /> 3. Well, before we went any further we had to confirm that the masquerade is upheld. Piper assured us that Charlie was a transient and unlikely to missed by anyone, and that she had made sure the body will not be found.<br /> <br /> Piper assured us that she was not withholding her blood from the late Charlie, and was in fact feeding him on a weekly basis, well in excess of his needs as a ghoul. However, she wasn't really letting him do anything other than sit at home and deliver her rent checks to the land lord. We tell her she is out of luck and move on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Bathtime</u></b><br /> <br /> Later that night, we had a meeting with our coterie. For those of you who may not have read the previous chapters, the other two members of Alice's and my coterie are Susan Small (ventrue, dragon, my cousin) and Christina (ventrue, invictus, my cousin.) They are both harpies and spend a lot of time in Elysium providing social cover for us while Alice and I separate the wheat from the chaff in the QZ.<br /> <br /> When the coterie meets to discuss strategy, we generally do it in the bathtub. The locked doors and running water prevent even Mouse from listening in. We aren't actually worried about Mouse going and blabbing our private business. However, vampires who might be reluctant to use dominate/majesty/auspex to get information out of citizens of Baltimore might not give a second thought to plucking such information from a ghoul. Better safe than sorry.<br /> <br /> We discussed three topics:<br /> <br /> 1. Elysium: As discussed, Christina's Elysium is not being built at nearly the same speed as other projects in the area. I had recently used Dominate 5 to spend the day at the construction site. I wanted to know what was happening. Basically the workers are arriving a few hours late and leaving a few hours early. They leave early to earn overtime working on other projects. They arrive late because they oversleep after working late on other projects.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, Belinsky isn't actually sabotaging us. He is just doing favors for others; making sure the limited supply of union labor is available to work overtime in Spider's territory, and Dorris Bette's territory, and Darren Soderberg's territory.<br /> <br /> Well... Susan, Alice and I begin discussing who we are going to sabotage in order to free up their share of the labor (Dorris Bettes obviously.) Christina doesn't like this idea. She has built her reputation in the city by being nice and being liked (which is easy to do when you are living under your mother's skirt [Octavia.]) Christina says she will just approach Spider and ask him to delay his projects so we can use his share of the labor pool, and in exchange she will help him financially with his projects at a later date. We let Christina win this one.<br /> <br /> 2. Christina's Inheritance: In the aftermath of Octavia's decision to leave the Invictus in favor of the Ordo Dracul, her assets were divided among the other Invictus members of the family. We wanted to know what Christina got so we could help her manage it. She got two main things:<br /> <br /> 2a. She was given control over many of Octavia's financial assets. I don't know how much, but I think it's safe to say 'lots.' Christina has asked for the help of our cousin Rosalyn Burnett who is an expert in both security and finance to help her manage her money and determine a budget. Cool beans.<br /> <br /> 2b. Christina has also been given domain over one of the city's best feeding grounds. There is a long and winding street which snakes through the territories of many other landholders. Most notably among them: Belinsky (nosferatu, invictus), Septimus (invictus, our uncle), Michael Seville (nosferatu priscus, carthian) and Dorris Bettes (daeva, carthian.) Dorris has been given control over a rather large chunk of Michael Seville's land. The best part of her territory borders Christina's new place in such a fashion where one side of the street is Christina's and the other belongs to Dorris. The street has many nightclubs, restaurants, art galleries, and the like. It is prime feeding territory. The territory includes only the properties that are *on* that street. It does not extend even one block over. What a nightmare it will be to defend.<br /> <br /> I asked Christina who decided what pieces she got. &quot;Why, Septimus of course.&quot; Grumble. Septimus has been increasingly pissed off about the actions of many members of the family (mostly me), but nothing has angered him more than Octavia's defection to the Ordo Dracul. This action effectively ended his bid to be the next prince. It is my belief that Septimus is setting Christina up to fail. I think he wants her new territory to be invaded so he can swoop in and take it for himself.<br /> <br /> We cannot allow this to happen. You see Christina is a bit of a wastrel who loves to pawn her work onto others. That is of course irrelevant. She is part of our coterie. Her failures will be our failures.<br /> <br /> In a perfect world, Christina would subinfeudate this land and gain for herself some vassals to defend it. Alice and I made a few recommendations as to who she might choose, but we gave each other a knowing look. We will probably have to intervene. In the meantime, we will assign Aika and Aiko to feed there, and keep their eyes open while they do it. It's a bandaid at best. The good news is that for a little while at least, Octavia's various retainers and influences are still there keeping the land secure. The bad news is that they will have to withdraw sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> 3. Felicity Fox: I had been content to let Felicity decide her own future covenant as long as she chose Invictus or Ordo Dracul. Now that Octavia (one of her main role models) had joined the Order, I felt it was a forgone conclusion that Felicity would join the Order as well, and while Alice and I could not spill the beans about our recent meeting with the Prince, that would not stop us from making preparations. We wanted Felicity out of the kiddie pool.<br /> <br /> So, I asked Susan to be her mentor in the coils of the dragon. If she learned even one, and was tested by the order she could gain citizenship in Baltimore. I chose Susan to be her mentor. Susan has a reputation as being a great teacher of coils and in particular a fast teacher of coils. In fact, she spent only 6 days in the kiddie pool when she was dropped there way back when. She was granted citizenship in Baltimore when she was able to verifiably teach a coil to a new student in 6 days.<br /> <br /> This is all great, but there is a problem: Susan already has two students, Scarlett and Kurt Hoffman. Scarlett (gangrel), Susan chose herself. Kurt, she took on as a student because Michael Seville asked for a boon so she would do it. Susan has said that she would continue to teach Kurt for as long as he would have her as a teacher. It's neither often nor easy to be owed a boon from Michael Seville.<br /> <br /> This problem isn't as simple as Susan taking a break from teaching Scarlett. If for some reason Robin (Scarlett's sister, apprentice to Enrique) were to learn more coils than Scarlett and be promoted above her, there would be serious drama. Well, I told Susan I would find a way to keep them both busy.<br /> <br /> 4. The Screening: Earlier this night, Alice decided to stop by the speakeasy in the kiddie pool which she and I helped to open during our residency there. The place functions as an informal Elysium and is currently being run by the coterie of my sister, Felicity Fox. Anyway, Alice went there and decided to spy on a carthian meeting that was happening in the movie theater which adjoined the speakeasy. Alice said she saw something interesting, and using Auspex shared her memory of the event with each of us in turn.<br /> <br /> 4a: Alice's memory: So, through Alice's eyes we can see that she is in a movie theatre (the same one where Michael Seville confronted Chibis (mekhet, deceased) a few halloweens ago. There is a TV/VCR on a rolling stand up front playing a tape of cartoons. Alice looks back and forth and we see that two carthians are giving each other some kind of signal. The one closer to the TV puts in a new video tape and hits play.<br /> <br /> On the TV screen are two actors, a black man and a white woman. The woman is on her hands and knees and the man is kneeling behind her as the two have sex. This must be Pascal's porno. As I am watching through Alice's memory I could just about swear that the woman in the film is Patricia Mason (daeva, invictus, member of my cousin Darren's coterie.) Another signal is given and the carthian by the TV pulls a hand held tape recorder from their hoodie and holds in on the TV stand before pressing play. They are trying to do this surreptitiously, but Alice spotted it.<br /> <br /> Moans and crys of &quot;Do it harder!&quot; now accompany the video. The voice is unmistakable. It is Patricia Mason's voice. At this point, Fred Black (nosferatu, invictus, member of my cousin Darren's coterie) comes walking into the movie theater. He stares transfixed at the screen with a look of shock on his face. After a few more minutes of pornography another signal is given. The tape is removed from the player and replaced. Soon the screen is filled with images of amateur claymation. Patricia Mason walks in.<br /> <br /> <b>Patricia</b> (smiling): &quot;Darren, hi! I'm glad you're here. I made a film and I wanted you to see it.&quot;<br /> She looks at the screen showing amateur claymation.<br /> <b>Patricia:</b> &quot;Oh, have you seen it already? Did you like it?&quot;<br /> <b>Darren:</b> &quot;You whore!&quot; He slaps Patricia across the face and storms out of the theater.<br /> Patricia leaves as well.<br /> <br /> And then I remembered that Alice had sent Mouse to investigate Pascal's new... hobby. So, we called for Mouse and once she had joined us in the tub (it's a big tub, but it's getting crowded now) she told us that she had a copy of the tape. So, four vampires and a ghoul march downstairs clad in robes to watch a porno. We rewind the tape and watch from the beginning. Here is what we learned:<br /> <br /> 1. The star of this movie is definitely not Patricia Mason, but someone must have gone to a lot of trouble to find someone who could pass for her from a certain angle and in a certain light.<br /> <br /> 2. At the beginning of the tape stage hands can been seen setting the scene, applying makeup to actors, and preparing the lighting. One of them we recognize as a ghoul belonging to Pascal Stitcher (mekhet, carthian, member of Dorris Bette's coterie.)<br /> <br /> So, we ask Mouse how she got the tape. Basically, she had a conversation with Pascal's ghoul when they were both at Elysium and he allowed her to make a copy of the tape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Damage Control</u></b><br /> <br /> So, Alice and I sent Susan and Christina home and we sent Aika and Aiko to see them safely to their destination. Susan tends to travel with heavy security, but Christina does not. Better safe than sorry. Anyway, Alice and I went to visit Patricia Mason as her house. We brought the tape with us. She was completely ignorant of the cruel joke played on her. All she knew was that a member of her coterie had slapped and called her a whore in a room full of carthians.<br /> <br /> We also told her we knew who was behind this attempted character assassination: members of Dorris Bette's coterie. (we later learned that it was Reaper's (daeva) idea and Pascal carried it out without the knowledge of Dorris Bette's.) In any event, Patricia now views Pascal and Reaper as enemies worthy of vengeance of some kind. We tell her that we would be happy to help with whatever she has in mind when the time comes.<br /> <br /> After Patricia's place, we traveled to Elysium. There, we asked Madeline Ross for permission to screen the full video, so as to dispel any nasty rumors from traveling farther than needed. So, we screened the video, in full, to anyone present who was willing to watch. Madame Ross agreed the film was crass, but she did enjoy seeing the schemes of carthians fail.<br /> <br /> Pascal's and Reaper's plan wasn't a complete failure. In fact, it was mostly a success. Sure, we mitigated the character assassination of Patricia Mason, but Patricia Mason has decided to leave the coterie which includes Fred Black and my cousin Darren Soderberg. So the coterie which controls land that borders Dorris Bettes' in the Locust Point Industrial Zone has been broken apart. This may make it easier for Dorris and her coterie to move against Darren's and Fred's territory.<br /> <br /> The ST told us he was surprised we sent Mouse to investigate this lead. If we had not done so, we wouldn't have gotten the tape immediately. There would have been a race against time to get the tape before it was destroyed, and that by the time we could show it to others in the city to defend Patricia's reputation, many would assume we had manufactured the tape ourselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ordo Dracul Apprentice Arrangements</u></b><br /> <br /> So, the next night Alice and I visited Antony (reeve, our boss.) Antony tells us that he is rotating us out of the Quarantine Zone for the time being to give us a little R&amp;R. We will be assigned to watch over the Inner Harbor (the kiddie pool) for awhile, and the trio of Auntie (daeva, invictus), Scarlett (gangrel, dragon), and Robin (gangrel, dragon) will be sent to the Quarantine Zone. This is welcome news. The inner harbor should be a little more mellow. The residents of the Inner Harbor have already been screened for rabies after all; many of them by Alice and me.<br /> <br /> Well, we thanked Antony for this news and told him that it would be advantageous for us if Scarlett and Robin were kept very busy for the next few months. Antony has no problems with that, and that should free up Susan's teaching schedule for Felicity. Yay!<br /> <br /> Felicity isn't the only one we are trying to bring into the Ordo Dracul:<br /> <br /> 1. Kyle (mekhet, our partner on the map quests.) has agreed to join the Order and to learn the Coils from me. We have been meeting on a weekly basis off screen for awhile now.<br /> <br /> 2. Patrick Brown (nosferatu.) Patrick has agreed to become an Ordo Dracul slave. I didn't offer to teach him because I already had an apprentice and because he and I do not get along well together. We are not enemies, we just rub each other the wrong way. Anyway, he had been a slave for awhile, but to my knowledge had not found a teacher. When I looked into the matter I found that Patrick had been trying to teach the coils to himself without a teacher.<br /> <br /> I felt that this was a dangerous path which could lead to a dangerous chrysalis. So, I spoke to my uncle Quintus (sworn of the dying light.) After all, what is and isn't an OK way to study the coils is certainly his business. After a few months I checked back. There was no change in the situation, so I informed Patrick of the danger of self teaching and asked if he had even tried to find a mentor. He had in fact asked every member of the Order to teach him (except me), but they all refused.<br /> <br /> I told Patrick that I would find him a mentor, or failing that I would teach him. Also around this time, I became aware that Steward Smiles (Patrick's Sire, invictus) was trying to get him to join Invictus. I also learned that he was sired by Steward in no small part because Steward thought he had the correct temperament to become an Invictus Knight.<br /> <br /> I took this information to Enrique (ventrue, sworn of the axe, my cousin.) Enrique is the only axe-sworn in the city. I told him that this could be an opportunity for him to find someone to help shoulder the burden. Enrique told me he would give Patrick another look.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Sophie's Problem</u></b><br /> <br /> So, one night as Alice and I are looking around the Kiddie Pool, we are approched by Sophie (nosferatu, unaligned.) Sophie is the one who long ago gave us a letter of introduction from Michael Seville which read simply &quot;ambitious, but inept.&quot; Anyway, Sophie tells us that she had a permission to create a ghoul and she thinks someone stole it. Furthermore, she wants help finding a candidate to make a ghoul. She has heard that vampires can be put to death if their ghouls make mistakes. We ask what kind of qualities she would want in a ghoul and Sophie tells us that she wants an older man who can pose as her father, &quot;...and no weird sex stuff, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, Alice and I travel across the bay looking for ghouls. After some looking around we discover that Piper Morgan has a new ghoul. The ghoul in question is an older black man wearing a suit and a bowtie. He reminds us of a member of the nation of Islam. When we ask her about her new ghoul, she shows us that she does in fact have permission to make one, and presents us with a piece of paper signed by Michael Seville. Hmm... I wasn't aware that creation of ghouls required written permission. Anyway, Piper tells us that she asked Kade (gangrel, dragon) to find her a candidate. Well, I assume that if Kade was granting a boon he would have done a good job vetting the guy. I thought this guy would probably fit the bill quite well for Sophie, and it was starting to look like Piper had Sophie's permission slip so...<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Have you already fed him? How many times?&quot;<br /> <b>Piper:</b> &quot;I've already fed him like 5 times. He is properly bound.&quot;<br /> <br /> Damn... It would have been really nice if we could have just handed this guy over to Sophie. Oh well.<br /> <br /> The long and short of this story is this:<br /> 1. Sophie asked Michael Seville for permission to create a ghoul and it was granted.<br /> 2. Sophie wanted something in writing so there would be no trouble for her. Seville gave her a piece of paper written in latin saying basically that if someone has a question about her making a ghoul they should come talk to him. The paper itself is not a permission slip, transferable or otherwise.<br /> 3. Piper bought the paper from Shaman (nosferatu) who bought it from Getter (deceased) who probably is the one who stole it from Sophie when he was still unliving.<br /> 4. Piper traded in good faith. She believed that she was purchasing a permission to make a ghoul all nice and legal, so we recommend that she not be in any trouble.<br /> 5. Sophie still has permission to create a ghoul. She just needs to find a candidate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Information from Seville</u></b><br /> <br /> When Alice and I went to Seville to inquire about the permission slip, our conversation wandered as it often does. Tonight, Seville asks what our opinion would be if he were to move into the inner harbor and take a chunk of the Kiddie Pool for himself. We tell him that we would not be in favor of that move. We think that 'contestable territory' is good for the city. It allows the young ones to learn, the angry ones to blow off steam, and the landless ones to travel. Further, once Seville makes such a move most or even all of the other Elders would want to take a piece of that pie for themselves and the kiddie pool would be no more.<br /> <br /> Seville tells us that with Octavia's exit from Invictus, it is all but settled that Peter (mekhet, invictus, Alice's grandsire) would be selected as the Invictus cadidate for next Prince. Because Seville is unwilling to tear the city apart with a civil war, he is content to scoop up as much territory as he can before the transition rather than wrestle for praxis after it.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;After all, Baltimore is just as much my city as it is the Prince's city. I have done just as much to shape this domain into what it is today.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Hasn't my Grandsire had a hand in shaping the city as well?&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Your grandsire has shaped his clan, his family, and his covenant certainly, but no... his influence on the city proper has been more modest.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville shared some really interesting information about the founders of the city.<br /> 1. Long ago the Prince was a very ambitious Invictus vampire.<br /> 2. Michael Seville (nosferatu priscus, Carthian) swore he would never rebel against the Prince as long as he was allowed the freedom and the territory to do his carthian social experiments.<br /> 3. Konrad Von Berg (ventrue priscus, Ordo Dracul) swore his allegiance to the Prince as long as the Prince allowed him the freedom to shape his clan and his family as he chose.<br /> 4. The Prince went looking for the right kind of vampire to be the daeva Priscus. Appolonia (daeva priscus, Crone) was chosen because she was content to be mostly apolitical.<br /> 5. The same can be said of the gangrel Priscus. Pilgrim (gangrel priscus, lancea sanctum) was sought out and recruited because he believed it was right for the church to play second fiddle to the invictus politically while the church concerned itself with souls.<br /> <br /> So, even as the Prince has enjoyed absolute monarchy for all this time, Michael Seville has been molding and shaping the city by molding and shaping the hearts and minds of the city's childer as they participate in the trial he created.<br /> <br /> According to Seville, if he is allowed to become Prince the city will look very much the same as it looks now. After all, vampires of every covenant have been sending their childer to run the gauntlet he created before they can be allowed to become 'citizens.'<br /> <br /> By contrast, Seville believes that if Peter has his way (and it won't be easy as he is not powerful enough to rule by fiat) that all immigrant vampires will be destroyed. Those that remain will find themselves living in a 'classical invictus setup: &quot;You know... all the lands divvied up, pretentious titles, boring parties.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, we asked Seville if he approved of the job we were doing. We had certainly made enemies among the newcomers to the city. But we felt the purpose of the Quarantine Zone was see the newcomers at their worst and check them for rabies. The only way to do that was to put them in a pressure cooker.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;If I did not approve of your methods you would be removed as my bailiffs. But you should realize something: The vampires who have arrived here from the council have lived their entire unlives in a world without trust. Dog eat dog, backstabbing culture between coteries all the while participating in an increasingly bloody conflict with werewolves. Do not expect them to arrive here and have the best table manners. Your job is to separate the ones who can be taught from the ones who cannot.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is kind of difficult for Alice and me. You see, we are both Marshals to Reeve Antony and Bailiffs to Michael Seville. When we are acting as Marshals, our authority is granted by Reeve Antony whose authority is granted by Peter, the seneschal/herald. When we are acting as Bailiffs, our authority is granted by Michael Seville. And sometimes, we are acting as both simultaneously.<br /> <br /> So we constantly have Peter whispering in one ear &quot;Kill them all,&quot; while Seville whispers in the other, &quot;Some of them are salvagable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice and Felix: tightrope walkers.<br /> <br /> We ask one more question before we leave. &quot;Aren't you angry with Dorris Bette's for encouraging this mass immigration?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Yes. I am. Her action forced us to alter the time table by several years. Allowing the werewolves to overrun that territory will require us to expend valuable blood to put things right again. There will be losses.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More to come. Thanks for reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way: Am I going into too much or too little detail? Am I fixating on certain details or conversations to the detriment of the write up? Are there things that don't make sense or I am not explaining well? Let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T08:42:59-07:00","id":691297,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the another amazing write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To answer your question, IMHO you're going into too little detail for sure, since I love these write-ups and could read them for hours at end <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/640-bram_pc","name":"Bram_pc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T11:01:18-07:00","id":694061,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here is an attempt at a more detailed play report.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Back Story 1</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I had recently approached Felicity and her coterie. We told Felicity that our duties would prevent us from watching over her like we have been. She should not expect as much support and protection as she has had in the past. I could tell she was worried, but what can I do? I don't think the Prince wants vampires who can't protect themselves as citizens.<br /> <br /> We also made a request of her coterie. The three of them have been running the unofficial Elysium known as the Speakeasy which Alice and I opened. They are the third group to run the place since it's opening, and we want them to close it. Not only do we want them to close it, but we want them to salt the earth so it won't be able to be reopened for a long time.<br /> <br /> Why? Well, soon Christina will open her Elysium in our territory, and there will be a period of time when the main city Elysium will be closed as it is moved at the order of the Prince. When that time comes, we don't want competition.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if you are wondering why the Prince has ordered the main Elysium to be moved, the ST told us out of character that because the Prince is courting invasion he knows that Elysium is likely to be attacked. He doesn't want the city museum with all its beautiful art to be sacked.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Back Story 2</u></b><br /> <br /> A while ago, Spider (nosferatu) had confessed to Felix that he thought my way of life was pretty cool. He wanted to find his own &quot;Alice&quot; and form a coterie of hot chicks. What can I say? Spider recognizes greatness when he sees it. He had also told me that he wasn't willing to just take anyone. He wanted someone cool and talented. To that end, he had his heart set on Patricia Mason (daeva, invictus.)<br /> <br /> Well, how convenient that Patricia has recently left her coterie. Well this is an opportunity if ever I've seen one. You see, I really would like to be able ensure the safety of my sister Felicity Fox, but I can't be everywhere at once. And now that Elliot Jr. is dead I no longer have an excuse to send Patrick Brown and the daeva twins to accompany Felicity's coterie on their diner's club.<br /> <br /> So, here's what I did. I told Spider that if he wanted a chance to get into Patricia's good graces he should consider keeping an eye on her childe, Nellie Stone. The kiddie pool can be dangerous. Sooner or later there may be an opportunity for him help Nellie and that might be a good ice breaker with Patricia.<br /> <br /> Nellie is in the same coterie as Felicity. If Spider is watching out for Nellie, he will be watching out for Felicity as well by proximity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Mekhet Meeting</u></b><br /> <br /> Tonight's meeting of the mekhetocracy is held as they often are at a pool at an old health club downtown. The pool is pleasantly heated and decorated in the Roman style. All mekhet of the city are present save the Archon Helen and the Seneschal, Peter. Also absent is Terry (carthian neonate.) There is a little small talk before we all disrobe and enter the pool. All this nudity isn't just for the sake of HBO style titillation. At mekhet meetings it is an unspoken statement that there are no secrets from the mekhetocracy.<br /> <br /> <b>Mary Sue:</b> &quot;It seems the warden of the east encountered a coterie of kindred and he failed to capture them. They have made their home somewhere in no man's land between fallow ground and Seville's holdings.<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;Did he tell you that?&quot;<br /> <b>Mary Sue:</b> &quot;We did not speak.&quot;<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;You're bad.&quot;<br /> <b>Mary Sue: </b>&quot;Are you using the children's vernacular? That cool is hot and bad is good?&quot;<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Terry </b>bursts into the room: &quot;Am I late?&quot;<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;No, you're just in time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Terry hastily disrobes and jumps into the pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Diana:</b> &quot;What was so important that you are late?&quot;<br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;You said I was on time!&quot;<br /> <b>Diana:</b> &quot;Well...&quot;<br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;I was in a meeting.&quot;<br /> <b>Diana:</b> &quot;A more important meeting than this one?&quot;<br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;I was meeting with Christina.&quot;<br /> <b>Ferdinand:</b> &quot;You've been very busy lately Terry. What have you been doing?&quot;<br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;Important things. Looking at places. I'm not ready to talk about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;I want to hear from Pascal.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Yes Pascal, how is your porn career going?&quot; There are chuckles from the room.<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;I think the interest in your career is Felix's alone.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Pascal </b>stands and bows: &quot;Thank you Alice. I see the error of my ways. I shall mend them.&quot;<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;A problem with keeping secrets is better discovered by friends than by enemies.&quot;<br /> <br /> All the vampires in the room: &quot;Thank you Alice.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;What are we thanking Alice for?&quot;<br /> <b>Lucien Du Lac</b>: &quot;One of Pascal's attendants had loose lips. Said things he shouldn't have said. Revealed plans he shouldn't have revealed.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Alice's attendant Mouse got Pascal's attendant to tell her about Pascal's plans last chapter. It doesn't matter that the plans revealed were minor in nature. A security leak is a security leak. Pascal will have to train his attendants better.)<br /> <br /> <b>Betty:</b> &quot;Am I the only one wondering why Peter is not present tonight?&quot;<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;We are not likely to see him very often for awhile. He is shouldering the burden of ruling the city.&quot;<br /> <b>Luis:</b> &quot;More than usual?&quot;<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;More than usual.&quot;<br /> <br /> The meeting is called to a close. We all get out of the pool and begin dressing. As we are dressing, we overhear a conversation between Simon (ancilla, archon, Lancea) and his childe Pascal. They are standing on the far side of the pool. I have to strain to hear, but I assume if they wanted privacy they would be having this conversation elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;Regarding your territorial dispute. Put reigns on it.&quot;<br /> <b>Pascal:</b> &quot;Why? Our plan worked.&quot;<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;I'm serious. Lay off the Bayside development project.&quot;<br /> <b>Pascal:</b> &quot;Are you giving an order or advice?&quot;<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;Advice. You're going to lose. You do realize who put the money down for that project, right?&quot;<br /> <b>Pascal:</b> &quot;Darren Soderberg (ventrue, invictus, censor, my cousin.) So what?&quot;<br /> <b>Simon:</b> &quot;So you're going to lose. Darren's duties as the censor keep him very busy. If Darren is unable to defend himself from your attacks because he is fulfilling his duties to the city, the Seneschal will intervene on his behalf. If Darren is not busy with his duties, he will handle the situation himself. Either way, you will lose. You are not at the same level of status or power in the city. Walk away from this fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is very interesting. Pascal is a member of Dorris Bette's coterie. Their coterie's land is bordered by that of Darren and his coterie, that of Antony the Reeve, and the territory of Alice's and my coterie. I suspect that the advice Simon just gave his childe could equally apply to Antony and his land. This means that Pascal and his friends are likely going to turn their attentions toward us. We better get prepared.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Preparations</u></b><br /> <br /> First we needed information. We met with Christina, but I wasn't in the mood to dance around the issues. I looked Christina in the eye and used my magic dominate powers to make her tell me the truth. No evasion. No bullshit. Just the facts ma'am. Christina spilled the beans about every last bit of her inheritance from Octavia. I did not erase her memory of the conversation. She was not too happy, but Alice and I were able to smooth it over.<br /> <br /> After our conversation, we took a drive up and down the long and winding street that is now Christina's territory while she pointed out the window. &quot;mine... mine... mine... that's mine too, etc.&quot; We asked Christina if she had figured out how she was going to defend her territory.<br /> <br /> <b>Christina:</b> &quot;I thought you sent the Aika and Aiko to feed there.&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;That is not a good long term solution.&quot;<br /> <b>Christina</b>: &quot;Well, Octavia's agents are still present all over.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;That won't last forever. Of course the Invictus will allow her influence to remain for the time being to ensure a smooth hand over, but after some time passes they will be wondering if Octavia really is going to relinquish her holdings.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, we took Christina to see her adopted brother Antony. You see, Antony was a neonate in the kiddie pool long before Alice and I were dropped there. During his trial, he walked into the Locust Point Industrial Area which were as barren as it comes and built an oasis in the desert in the form of a trendy gentrified neighborhood with an active nightlife. He has held this territory for a few decades. I figured perhaps he would have some good advice for Christina.<br /> <br /> Alice and I waited for Christina outside Antony's bar while she talked to him. Alice and I both have obfuscate 5 (cloak the gathering version.) It took some convincing to get Alice to learn it too, but it allows us to travel with our various retainers and friends with an added level of security. So, as we were escorting Christina invisibly back to our haven we noticed Sam Wagner (nosferatu, QZ resident) moving through our territory. he looked like he was in a hurry. When I popped out and asked him what he was up to, he broke out into a run. Because Christina was with us, we let him go. We know where to find him later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Kade are you out there? It's me Felix</u></b><br /> <br /> A long time ago, when Alice and I were first starting to consider becoming landowners we made an agreement with Kade (gangrel, dragon.) Kade and his vampire girlfriend Lorraine (daeva, dragon) have long had ambitions to extend their influence in the seedy world of organized crime, which has until now been the undisputed domain of Belinsky (nosferatu, invictus, client of Septimus.) They do have influence amongst several street level gangs, but nothing like the mafia.<br /> <br /> When Alice's and my coterie was awarded land on the Locust Point Peninsula I was surprised that Kade did not put his name in the hat to get some as well. When we spoke on the matter, Kade told me that he was focused on other things at the time and there were no hard feelings. If he wanted that land, he would have played for it. He also said that he would be willing to develop the criminal aspects of our territory when the time came. Well, we have had this territory for awhile now... and I have yet to see hide nor hair of Kade or Lorraine.<br /> <br /> Well, I thought it would be good to have friendly criminal assets on the ground before Dorris and her coterie begin their attack on our territory.<br /> <br /> So, I arranged a meeting with Kade, Lorraine, Alice and me. I asked Kade why he wasn't moving on the territory. At first he gave me a line about being patient, it not being the right time, and not wanting to stunt the growth of the local economy by moving gangs in and starting protection rackets. Lorraine was impatient as well, and took my inquiry as her cue to push Kade to act more quickly. Together, Lorraine, Alice and I were able to get Kade to tell us the real reason for his inaction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kade:</b> &quot;There is a war coming. I want to preserve my strength and my assets for when they are really needed.&quot; According to Kade, the Order has been recruiting both soldiers and officers. &quot;I'm not the only one paying attention. If I have noticed, other people have noticed.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Kade says the Order has been recruiting soldiers and officers, he means Alice and I have been recruiting them. Alice and I have been the driving force which has transformed the Order in Baltimore from a small coterie of navel gazers into a covenant with the potential to be a martial threat to any of the other covenants in the city. Following is a quick recap of our recruiting efforts:<br /> <br /> 1. We expended no small amount of effort to convince Kade, who had remained unaligned for nearly a century to join the Order. Kade is nearly ancilla age, an awesome fighter, but more important has an awesome mind.<br /> 2. Pushed for Robin and Scarlet to be promoted from Slave to Supplicant and be made citizens of the city. The gangrel sisters are both combat capable individuals.<br /> 3. Convinced Kyle, who was being recruited into the Carthian Movement that the Order is better suited to his talents and temperament. I have been personally training him in the Coil of Blood. Don't forget that all mekhet in the city are stone cold killers.<br /> 4. We pursued and recruited Patrick Brown who has balls of steel and an expert command of the nightmare discipline.<br /> 5. Octavia. Prior to joining the Order, Octavia was one of the highest ranking Invictus vampires in the city. She is old, powerful, ambitious, and competent. But most important of all. She is wise. She is the piece of the puzzle that probably has other factions in the city worried the most, as she could lead our newly formed army.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget that Alice and I are not exactly slouches in the violence department. Neither are Enrique or Luis, and I would bet money that Michael Seville's childe Kurt Hoffman is also combat ready. (In fact I have seen him in a fight once already.)<br /> <br /> Kade was also worried that Octavia was planning to attack his sire, Sharon Winter. If this were to come to pass, it would be really awkward considering both Kade and Sharon had sworn their fealty to Octavia during her invictus days. Both of them had an opportunity to leave Octavia's service when she jumped ship for the Ordo Dracul, but neither of them took it. I assured Kade that no such attack was coming.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;No, Octavia has no plans to attack your sire's holdings. Why would she? You are both her allies. But your instincts are good. Octavia is ambitious, competent... and landless.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't often throw my weight around and give orders. I am after all just an unsworn scholar of hunger. In this case I did order Kade (supplicant of hunger) and Lorraine (Slave) to maintain secrecy. Oh, and Lorraine told us that she has learned the first coil of blood from Kade. She is just waiting to get tested and promoted.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after a discussion we all agree that Christina's newly inherited land is both our least defended and most valuable asset at this time. We think that if Dorris is going to strike, she will do it there. Kade agrees to move into the area. Unlike our territory in Locust Point, Christina's inheritance is fully developed and thriving.<br /> <br /> <b>Kade:</b> &quot;There is a lot of nightlife on that street. We'll start by making sure as many of the clubs as possible have bouncers that are our people. We will start probing, finding out which cops take bribes and which ones don't. We will push out any drug dealers in the area who aren't controlled by us, but none of them will be made aware of the supernatural in general or of us in specific. They will be separated from us by at least a few degrees, so if some dealer gets busted for selling coke in the ladies room we can replace him and move on. Finally, we will get involved in private security and we will have that street locked up tight.&quot;<br /> <br /> Kade regards our relationship as a long term business partnership. He is not asking for boons to do this. We are giving him an opportunity to get involved in organized crime which is a step up from street gangs, and he will certainly make some good money doing it. We get to focus our efforts on building Christina's Elysium while Kade watches our back. Win win.<br /> <br /> Also? Septimus, who has set Christina up to fail is probably going to shit a brick. Fun.<br /> <br /> We weren't the only ones who have made arrangements to safeguard Christina's inheritance. Christina made a deal with Steward Smiles (nosferatu, invictus) to keep an eye on her lands in exchange for permission to feed there.<br /> <br /> After we cleared the deal with Christina we spoke to Octavia to let her know the presence of her agents was no longer required in the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Octavia:</b> &quot;Good luck, and don't forget the motto.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Take all you can. Give nothing back.&quot;<br /> <br /> Octavia nodded and smiled proudly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Oaths, Great and Small</u></b><br /> <br /> Well, I was feeling pretty good about the previous night's transaction. I felt that it gave us a chance to breathe. It led me to thinking about the Ordo Dracul and how I wanted to ensure our family's dominance in it. Alice and I had surely made great strides by convincing Octavia to join. She would almost certainly be offered the oath of the Mysteries one day. This ensures that even when Konrad one day succumbs to torpor, our family will still have a voice within the suborder.<br /> <br /> Alice and I had set our sights on the Sworn of the Dying Light. We are disqualified from joining the Mysteries due to our mutual blood bond, and neither of us are willing to swear an oath which requires us to potentially fight and die to protect any member of the order, even those who we may not like. Susan once suggested that we take the Oath of the Axe, and when push came to shove we could interpret the oath in a more self serving way.<br /> <br /> <b>Alice</b>: &quot;I will not swear a false oath.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice would actually prefer to join the Sworn of the Mysteries and is a little disappointed that we may not join. I am not disappointed. I feel that joining the Dying Light will offer us the greatest potential for autonomy. After our apprenticeship, we will become journeymen. At that point we will be free to pursue our own agendas for transcendence. And while it won't prevent us from fighting for the Order if we so choose, it will not require us to protect any old vampire who happens to have learned a coil.<br /> <br /> Why do I bring this up? Because I have a vision. When all is said and done, I want to see Konrad, Octavia, and Susan swear the oath of the Mysteries. I want Alice and I to join Quintus in the Dying Light, and I want to see Enrique recruit vampires who do not share our blood ties to help him shoulder the burden of the Axe. Perhaps in the future I will take one for the team and groom/sire a vampire with the idea that they will join the Axe as well, but that's distant future stuff now.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Susan has always been an up and comer in the covenant. Her excellent teaching abilities are well documented, and she has recently developed a new coil. Well not so much developed a new coil but managed to teach herself an existing coil which no one else in the region has knowledge of by reading about it. Susan has taught herself one of the Treasures of Mae Ji (upadana/loose the bonds of attachment.) She has yet to announce it to the covenant, but she has shared with us the information. Were she to inform Konrad or Quintus of this discovery she would be able to write her own ticket and take one of the Great Oaths.<br /> <br /> Well, her discovery is impressive, but I feel that her true talent lies in social strategy. She was a key player in formulating our plan to manipulate Elliot Jr. into diablerizing his own sire all those years ago. I think her mind would be a great addition to the Mystery Sworn of the city.<br /> <br /> So, we visited Susan and asked her what her plans were. She was aware that she could at this point probably be admitted to either organization based on her merits and has considered them both, but ultimately she wants to join the Dying Light. Why?<br /> <br /> <b>Susan Small:</b> &quot;If I join the Sworn of the Mysteries, I will always be fourth. Konrad is first, and after him Bartolomew. It's only a matter of time before Octavia is offered to join them, and then there would be me: Little Susan. On the other hand, if I join the Dying Light there is only Quintus higher than me. Eventually he will take a long torpor nap and then I will be on top. Numero Uno.&quot;<br /> <br /> We try to convince Susan that joining the Mysteries will not prevent her from continuing to explore her experiments, but that joining the Dying Light will certainly lessen her ability to steer the covenant as a whole. We also argue that having three family members in the Mysteries will ensure continuity of leadership. I share my vision of the Order with Susan but she still won't budge. Eventually she makes us an offer:<br /> <br /> <b>Susan</b>: &quot;I will pursue the Oath of the Mysteries if you help me get a blood bond on Christina.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh for fuck sake! ... Grumble. I tell her that Octavia will not be happy if she tries that.<br /> <br /> Susan's argument in favor of her blood bonding Christina goes like this:<br /> 1. Christina has just inherited a lot of territory and a lot of money and lost a certain amount of cover because of Octavia's loss of status. &quot;I bet there are others out there right now saying to themselves, 'she's rich and cute, what a wonderful pokemon she will make.'&quot;<br /> 2. Christina is not very serious about her security. &quot;If she was bonded to me, I could convince her to get more ghouls and security and stuff.&quot;<br /> 3. &quot;I'm in love with her. She completes me. I need her to keep me happy. I know I can convince her that gender doesn't matter now that we are vampires&quot; (Susan is gay. Christina is straight.)<br /> 4. Look at you and Alice. It's working for you.<br /> <br /> We tell Susan that our situation is a lot different from what she describes, not the least of which reason is we fell in love, got married, and mutually decided to drink each other's blood. One of us wasn't tricked by the other.<br /> <br /> Finally, I grow tired of the bullshit and tell her so. She tells us the real truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Susan:</b> &quot;I'm worried I'm going to end up like my sire and grandsire. Rosalyn and Quintus are so calcified. Their feelings are so dull. I can already see the cobwebs of torpor forming around Quintus and I know they made me that way. I need Christina to keep the fire burning in my soul!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't even know what to do about this one. Sigh...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Followup</u></b><br /> <br /> A few nights later Alice went out on her own. I decided to check in with Patrick Brown (nosferatu) and see if Enrique decided to begin teaching him or if I would have to make good on my promise. So, I stopped by his haven and knocked on the door. The door was slightly ajar and opened further due to my knocking. I walked in to look for Patrick, but he wasn't home. I couldn't tell what, but I felt something was off.<br /> <br /> I'm generally not one to panic, so I decided to visit the speakeasy and ask if anyone has seen Patrick Brown. I asked a few people and no one had seen him for a few days. So I headed downstairs where I found Kurt Hoffman (nosferatu, childe of Seville, ordo dracul slave) gearing up for a fight. He and two ghouls were checking their weapons and getting ready to roll.<br /> <br /> I ask Kurt what's happening. He hasn't seen Nellie Stone (daeva, childe of Patricia Mason) for awhile either and he thinks something bad has happened to her. I asked if he would mind if we tagged along (Alice was busy doing something for the mekhetocracy that night, but I did bring Sidney and Banjo the wonderdog.) Together, we checked a few sites in the area with no luck.<br /> <br /> The third location we checked was the public library which sits of the border separating the kiddie pool with downtown. It was about 2am when we arrived. The library was closed but the doors were unlocked. Sidney, Banjo, and I moved quickly into the library (obfuscate 5) while Kurt and his ghouls took a more cautious pace. We heard sounds of a struggle and when we reached the center of the library we were treated to the following scene:<br /> <br /> Nellie Stone is bound, gagged, and tied to a chair. There are four mortal thugs on the ground around her in states ranging from beaten down to beaten unconsciou. Spider (nosferatu, childe of Boris) is wrestling with a vampire wearing a ski mask. Spider appears to have sustained more injuries than his opponent, but he is slowly gaining the upper hand. I appear behind his opponent and pull him off Spider and Sidney helps me to unmask him. It is Fred Black (nosferatu, invictus)<br /> <br /> Fred wriggles free of our grasp and runs away. I am prepared to give chase, but decide to stay with Spider. Sidney and Banjo are sent to search the library in case there are witnesses that need to be dealt with. Better safe than sorry. Kurt arrives. He wastes no time in freeing Nellie Stone from her bonds before he and his ghouls whisk her away. He did return about 20 minutes later, by which time Spider and I had wrangled the mortal thugs into one of the study rooms and were questioning them under the influence of Dominate. Here is what we learned:<br /> <br /> 1. They were hired by Fred Black (they don't know him by name) to kidnap the girl (Nellie.)<br /> 2. They brought her here as instructed before they were attacked by Spider.<br /> 3. It wasn't until Spider had disabled them that Fred attacked Spider.<br /> 4. They have day jobs: Framing and drywalling. Hey, we are short on construction workers so I offer them a job. Waste not want not, right? (Don't worry, my overuse of Dominate will smooth things over.)<br /> <br /> Alice and I later spoke with Patricia to make sure she knew the details of the situation. She wanted to know why Fred would do this and asks Alice to find out for her.<br /> <br /> <b>Patricia:</b> &quot;I do not plan to deal with this in the courts so...&quot;<br /> <br /> So... there is no legal reason why Alice should not just pluck the info from the mind of Fred Black. Alice did so and confirmed what I had suspected to be true: Fred Black kidnapped Nellie Stone (Patricia's childe) with the intention that he would be the one to 'rescue' her in an effort to get back into the good graces of his former coterie-mate. I don't think it worked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Sidetracked</u></b><br /> <br /> It's great that everything turned out well where Nellie is concerned. That doesn't change the fact that I haven't been able to find Patrick Brown. So Alice and I went to see Enrique (scholar of Sanguine Pain, Sworn of the Axe) who not too long ago said he would consider taking Patrick on as a student.<br /> <br /> <b>Enrique:</b> &quot;I offered to take him on as a student, but the little ingrate didn't show up for his first lesson.&quot;<br /> <br /> From there, Alice and I traveled to Patrick's haven. She looked at Patrick's haven and with her superior investigation skills and auspex and was able to get a better idea of what happened here than 'something's not right.'<br /> <br /> Alice finds that someone moved a rug to cover bullet holes and blood stains. They used carpenters wood glue to fill the holes. We canvas the apartment building. The long and short of it is this:<br /> <br /> A girl who lives alone heard a commotion downstairs. When she got up the courage to check it out, she found Patrick Brown unconscious (torpid) riddled with bullet holes. His body had been dragged in front of an east facing window and left there with his fangs clearly visible. The window coverings had been torn off the frame. She put two and two together and figured that Patrick was a vampire. Fortunately for us, she reads those books about girls who fall in love with vampires. She is under the impression that when Patrick wakes up they are going to fall in love and he will make her a vampire.<br /> <br /> Some simple steps are taken. The girls memories are changed a bit, and I make a mental note to reward her for her good deed in the future. Patrick's body is recovered from under the girl's bed and is taken to the chapter house to ride out his torpor. Patrick is a neonate. I don't expect his slumber to last too long.<br /> <br /> When he wakes up, hopefully he can tell us who did this to him and we can go piss in their cheerios until they die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Foster Parents</u></b><br /> <br /> So, Felix and Alice have really busy unlives. Sometimes I wonder if we will be able to deal with a more leisurely pace when one day comes that the transition of the Prince's throne is complete. Currently, in addition to our duties as Marshals to the City and Bailiffs to Michael Seville we are acting as mentors:<br /> <br /> Alice is mentoring Kade in the Coil of the Blood. He learned his first coil from a suspicious source and she wanted to make sure that everything was on the up and up for him and by extension for Lorraine (who Kade is mentoring.)<br /> <br /> Felix is mentoring Kyle (mekhet) in the coil of the blood. He is also mentoring Sherry (daeva) so that she can be given over to Appolonia one day.<br /> <br /> I really didn't think Alice would be in favor of us taking on Seville's potential childe, but when I broached the topic she gave her blessing without reservation. Her reasoning was pretty much identical to that of Susan Small when she was given an opportunity to teach Michael Seville's childe (Kurt Hoffman) the coils of the dragon. (It is not often that one is given an opportunity to be owed a boon from Michael Seville.)<br /> <br /> So, we travelled to Seville's office to tell him of our decision.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;We have decided to take you up on your offer.&quot;<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Which one?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville has made us several offers, including to work for him directly which would require us to convince Octavia to either swear her fealty to him or release us to his service. We are happy where we are in any event. We specify that we are going to groom his future childer.<br /> <br /> Seville takes us to see our new ward. He is asleep at a house a 20 minute drive away. We enter an older house and descend into the basement. There is man in his early 20's asleep. When he is woken by Seville he refers to him as 'grandfather.' Anyway, he has long black hair, a metallica t-shirt, and a backpack. Seville leaves and we take the dood home.<br /> <br /> Once there, we begin with our patented Dominate/Auspex tag team interrogation to make sure what we see is what we get. It turns out the kid has known for a long time that he may one day be chosen to begin a new life as an immortal. Well that simplifies some things. Anyway, I decide that I am not in the mood to sugar coat things. If the guy is expected to learn to think like Alice and me, he should learn what it is like to *be* Alice and me.<br /> <br /> So, I take the guy to the games room and rifle through the bookshelves. Then I open three jigsaw puzzles and dump their combined pieces on the floor before crouching down and mixing them up.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Alice and I are going out. You have until dawn to assemble these three puzzles and put a healthy breakfast on the table for Sidney and Mouse. If you fail there will be consequences.&quot;<br /> <br /> I thought that was an apt metaphor for many of the situations that have happened in Alice's and my life together. And then the doorbell rang.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Ransom</u></b><br /> <br /> We have a visitor. It is Steward Smiles (nosferatu, invictus, sire of Patrick Brown.) Well I don't let him speak immediately. I am pretty sure I know why he is here. I tell him that there was an attempt on Patrick's life, and that his torpid body is safely interred.<br /> <br /> <b>Steward:</b> &quot;Then why would they send me this?&quot;<br /> <br /> Steward hands us a ransom note in the classic style (letters cut out of newspapers and magazines glued to paper.) It tells Steward that they have his childer and that he should bring an unspecified amount of cash to a location across the bay in the Quarantine Zone.<br /> <br /> Before we went off half cocked, we confirmed that Patrick was in fact safely resting at the Chapter House. Enrique had moved him to an area that is not accessible by the unsworn, but I was able to get Bartholomew (daeva, sworn of the mysteries) to confirm Patrick's presence. He was there.<br /> <br /> At this point, I am thinking we have a not fully thought out scheme of some stupid newcomer in the QZ. Well, I have a plan. A long time ago, when Alice and I were still in the kiddie pool we filled paint ball guns with pepper balls and paint balls filled with that purple dye that banks use in dye packs to mark robbers. Well, I still had the barrel of dye in the basement (I wasn't able to get it in smaller portions) and the paintball equipment.<br /> <br /> When we arrived home, Seville's recruit had completed all three puzzles and there was an omelet on the kitchen counter. Cute. I was not distracted by that. Instead I decided to draft the guy into our little gang. He just experienced a metaphorical taste of our existence. Now he could have a real taste.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Plan</u></b><br /> <br /> Around the time when we acquired Aika and Aiko, I convinced Alice to spend her precious XP to also get obfuscate 5, so that on the (many) occasions when she left me to go do mekhety spy stuff she could bring backup with her in case things went sideways. This is relevant to the plan thusly:<br /> <br /> 1. Alice and I would each follow Steward Smiles to the ransom drop point leading a small group of obfuscated fighters. Alice would take Aika and Mouse. I would take Aiko, Sidney, and New Guy (Seville's thrall. He refuses to use his mortal name and he wants us to come up with one for him. We haven't. yet.)<br /> <br /> 2. Steward will lure the 'kidnappers' in while Alice and I set up a cross fire.<br /> <br /> 3. We will all open fire on the 'kidnappers' marking them with purple bank dye.<br /> <br /> 4. We will move in and kick their asses.<br /> <br /> 5. Any who manage to escape our ass kicking will be marked. We can find them later and make sure they get the ass kicking they deserve.<br /> <br /> Sounds awesome right? We thought so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Execution</u></b><br /> <br /> We travelled across the bay following Steward. The ransom location was not quite a warehouse. It was much larger, and there was a corrugated tin roof to keep the maze of crates and shipping containers dry, but there were not walls, just beams to hold it up. Deep into the yard, we can see lights. Steward heads in that direction and we follow.<br /> <br /> As Steward nears the lights, we see that the ground is covered in sand. No... that's not right. There is a peculiar texture and smell to it. Well... I failed my science roll, and Alice has no dots in science. Fortunately for us, New Guy succeeded on his roll. This is not sand. It is a mix of powdered aluminum and iron oxide which has been spread far and wide over the ground of about one half of the area under the roof. New Guy grabs me by the arm. He looks frightened and points at the ground. I get another science roll and realize we are in deep shit. Aluminum and iron oxide, if ignited are extremely flammable and burn really hot. Fuck.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;FIRE TRAP! RUN!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> We run. Alice runs. Steward runs. As we are running, We notice there are men standing on the rooftops of the adjacent buildings. The one closest to Alice's group raises his gun arm which is holding a flare gun. Before he can shoot he is hit by several paintballs and pepper balls. This is enough to throw off his aim and his flare goes wide, falling harmlessly toward the water. So, instead of being surrounded by fire on all sides we are surrounded on only three. Miraculously, no one frenzies and no one dies. Lucky die rolls.<br /> <br /> We are unable to capture any of the assailants, so we withdraw to a safe distance and wait. Across the street from the storage yard there is a car in an alley. Inside that car is Trenton (daeva, carthian.) He sits there looking at his watch. We sit there watching him. After about 90 minutes, he gets out of his car. We follow him back into the storage yard, which by now has burned itself out. When he reaches the edge of what was the field of aluminum and rust he drops his flashlight and runs. We let him.<br /> <br /> So... I'm more than a little pissed. We all leave the area and meet back at Alice's and my haven. Before we do anything else, we call Darren Soderberg. Darren is my cousin and he holds the office of city Censor. He is specialized in responding to potential breeches of the masquerade. I think an arson investigation that could be traced back to a vampire qualifies as such an event.<br /> Darren will have the contacts and influence to either shut down or misdirect the investigation before it becomes a problem for us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Playing a Hunch</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I are going to find out who just tried to kill us, and we are going to make them suffer. We spend some time looking into sources where one could get large amounts of the chemicals needed to set this up. And as we were looking into all this, we just had a feeling that we should be talking to Terry. Terry the mekhet is a carthian and she spends a lot of her time helping other carthians and neonates get the things they need. For example, a long time ago Alice and I were looking for old arcade games for cheap to put into the speakeasy. Terry introduced us to the owner of a junkyard who collected more than just scrap metal.<br /> <br /> So, we paid a visit to Terry's place and asked her if she had helped anyone get their hands on large quantities of either of the chemicals in question.<br /> <br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;Are they going to be in trouble?&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;Yes. Lots of it.&quot;<br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;He said he was selling it for money.&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;That's not what they did with it.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Terry, you need to realize that not all carthians are cool and trustworthy like Michael Seville. A lot of them are assholes like whoever tricked you into helping them so they could try to murder us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Terry gave us a name: Sam Wagner (nosferatu, carthian)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Resolution</u></b><br /> <br /> We brought this information to the Reeve (Antony.) Then we gathered as much muscle as we could. Our Posse included the following kindred:<br /> <br /> Enrique (ventrue, sworn of the axe)<br /> Auntie (daeva, marshal, invictus)<br /> Scarlett (gangrel, dragon, marshal)<br /> Robin (gangrel, dragon, marshal)<br /> Antony (ventrue)<br /> Felix Fox (that's me)<br /> Alice Fox (everyone's favorite mekhet)<br /> Kade (gangrel, dragon)<br /> <br /> We also arrived with a mess of ghouls. With this show of force, there was not violence. We took Sam Wagner and all his ghouls to an off grid location owned by Antony. None of the other carthians stood up for him. We also picked up Trenton.<br /> <br /> Both vampires and all their ghouls were separated for interrogation. Here is the outcome:<br /> 1. Wagner maintained his innocence.<br /> 2. He changed his tune when we found that one of his ghouls had welts and purple dye all over his chest. We had succeeded in marking him. Sweet.<br /> 3. Sam then confessed that the 'dark lord' had been whispering to him and made him do it. The dark lord again? wtf!?!<br /> 4. We are pretty sure that Sam was under the effects of a mental discipline of some kind. Probably Nightmare.<br /> 5. Trenton was the patsy. He was hired to pick up the cash nothing more.<br /> 6. The archons arrive and Sam Wagner is put to the final death.<br /> 7. Trenton is given a strike. (the Reeve has a three strikes and you're dead policy for QZ residents.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Mercs</u></b><br /> <br /> After all this excitement, Alice and I met with Marco and Polo. They have been in the QZ for a few months now and in that time we have known them to be mercenaries. They will take cash money and do jobs. Usually people pay them a few hundred bucks and they get a few hundred bucks worth of effort, but they have never reneged on a contract. We also had new information from Sherry about their capabilities.<br /> <br /> We weren't going to assume that the recent attack was specifically aimed at us (it probably was.) It might have been aimed at the Ordo Dracul. After all, Scarlett and Robin (the other marshals) and Patrick (the nearly killed vampire) are all members of the order. So, Alice and I paid Marco and Polo $10K to watch out for Sunny (daeva, dragon, QZ resident.) We will see what kind of effort they put forth when they are paid less modest sums.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Book Keeping</u></b><br /> <br /> Several vampire residents of the QZ have passed their rabies tests and will be granted permission to move into the inner harbor. They are:<br /> <br /> Piper Morgan (daeva, Carthian)<br /> Patrick (not Patrick Brown, mekhet, carthian)<br /> Shaman (nosferatu Carthian)<br /> Marco and Polo (daeva, carthian) This will make it harder for them to do their job, but I'm not going to lie and say they aren't ready to move on. We have some integrity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks again for reading. This brings things up to date. It will be a few weeks before I have anything new to post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T01:53:29-07:00","id":718154,"title":"","content":"Ey! I got late to the posts, dammit. And i have no time to answer properly now,so i'll leave this here,quickly, and will come later. I love the posts as they are written, but if you manage to give them more detail, all the best for me! Keep up the good work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:39:22-07:00","id":897846,"title":"","content":"Hi guys. I've been gone for a while, but we recently got together and played a game of Vampire! I had great time and hope to be writing the Kiddie Pool Saga part 9... soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:50:51-07:00","id":897988,"title":"","content":"Yay!! Welcome back!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:57:25-07:00","id":898258,"title":"","content":"Seconded! My favourite vampire AP is back on track!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:34:55-07:00","id":900213,"title":"","content":"I couldn't find my notes from the last game, which was months ago. So, here from memory is a summary of the few scenes I remember. I hope to get started on part 9 soon. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Situation:</u></b><br /> <br /> It has been even longer than usual since my last post. Please allow me to summarize the current setup.<ul><li>The Prince is presumed dead by the residents of the Quarantine Zone, who are becoming increasingly unruly.</li> <li>The Northeast territory of Baltimore has been abandoned by Ryan, its Warden, leaving the bus station (one of the city's major entry points) unwatched and undefended.</li> <li>Alice and Felix are still serving as Marshals to Antony who is both Reeve of the city and Bailiff to Michael Seville.</li> <li>The Locust Point Industrial Zone (LPI) has been divided amongst several coteries, including ours. The territorial borders are not fixed just yet though, and the aforementioned coteries are competing for the biggest slice of the pie they can get their hands on.</li> </ul><b><u>Our Coterie:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Alice Fox:</b> Mekhet, Scion of the bloodline of the Prince of Baltimore. Wife of Felix.<br /> <b>Felix Fox:</b> Ventrue, Grande-childe of Konrad Von Berg (ventrue Priscus) Husband of Alice.<br /> <b>Christina:</b> Felix's cousin. Harpy.<br /> <b>Susan Small: </b>Felix's cousin. Great Grand-Childe of Konrad Von Berg. Harpy.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Our Plans:</u></b><br /> <br /> We are currently attempting to juggle the responsibilities of being Marshals of the city, while developing our territory in the LPI. There are to be two jewels in the crown of our territory.<br /> <br /> 1. The Foxhole: A cosplay club that will open soon, and be managed by Kat (gangrel, carthian, cosplayer.) It will hopefully become a great feeding ground for us.<br /> <br /> 2. Elysium: We have secured permission from the Master of Elysium to create an official city Elysium within our territory. It is also currently under construction.<br /> <br /> The Elysium will need staff. Lots of staff. We plan to leverage our coterie's three ventrue dominate powers to make our Elysium into a dollhouse, with lots of dolls to play with. Well, humans who won't be missed aren't too easy to find the numbers we need.<br /> <br /> You might be thinking that the homeless population would be a good pool from which to draw. However, the over reliance on them for feeding in the Kiddie Pool and Quarantine Zone has fostered a belief amongst many homeless that there is a serial rapist of the homeless in the city. Many of them have banded together for protection.<br /> <br /> In talking about this, Alice and I have concluded that the Bus Station would be the best source of 'staff.' It brings fresh bodies into the city nightly, many of them transients and runaways. Their disappearances would be relatively easy to cover up. So, we decided to propose to the powers that be to exert their influence to get the bus station moved from its current (unattended) location, to a new location within our coterie's territory. The benefit to us is we can steer likely candidates to staff our Elysium. The benefit to the city is we will keep an eye out at the bus station for new vampire arrivals into the city. Win-win, right?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Alice and I have spoken on this topic with Septimus (my uncle), Peter (schenescal, Alice's Grandsire), and Michael Seville (elder, nosferatu Priscus) off and on. However, before any kind of agreement could be reached...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Summons</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I are served with summonses to appear before a court at Elysium. Well... being made to appear at court is not good in the best of circumstances, but it is even worse to be blind-sided. Alice and I do a little asking around in advance so we can form some kind of strategy before appearing in court, but Michael Seville advises us to let it ride.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Court</u></b><br /> <br /> So, Alice and I arrive at Elysium at the appointed hour and are led to a large meeting room to find out what is going on. We are seated in a room packed with vampires, most of them Carthian. Pilgrim (gangrel priscus, archbishop) is presiding, and Dorris Bettes (neonate, daeva, carthian) is the plaintiff. Pilgrim calls the meeting to order, and Dorris stands.<br /> <br /> <b>Dorris:</b> &quot;I have asked you here to discuss the contest over the land in the Locus Point Industrial Area. I believe that the coterie of Alice and Felix Fox are unfairly influencing the outcome of the competition using their family connections. They have already done this to make sure the metro station will be within their territory, and now they doing same with the bus station. I would move that a judgment be rendered preventing the use of outside influence in this competition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pilgrim waves over an assistant who hurries out of the room. He returns in a few minutes with Septimus and Peter.<br /> <br /> <b>Peter: </b>&quot;Madame Bettes, I have heard your complaint against Mr. and Mrs. Fox, and I think you are operating under a false assumption. First, the apportionment of territory to neonate coteries is not some kind of gameshow or contest. The placement of the Bus Station, or any other thing in this city will not be decided by competition or committee. It will be decided based on what is best for Baltimore.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Peter:</b> &quot;Second, the Bus Station is an entry point into the city which can be used and exploited by our enemies. It must be watched and defended. Felix Fox and Alice Fox have shown that they have not only the necessary skills and resources, but also the nerve and commitment to defend this city against outsiders. You have yet to show these qualities, fledgling.&quot;<br /> <br /> The smug smile worn by Doris at the beginning of the scene is replaced with a look of mortified embarrassment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 05-26-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:22:04-07:00","id":900659,"title":"","content":"Two questions<br /> <br /> 1. Why was the territory around the bus station abandoned by Ryan?<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. What was the outcome of the request for judgement prohibiting the use of undue family influence to control how the borders are drawn up? If it's not a contest (except it is) and the territories are being assigned based on what's best for the city (code word for personal favorites), why bother with the pretense of allowing the Carthians to erroneously believe they are getting anything at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:27:00-07:00","id":900994,"title":"","content":"Two answers<br /> <br /> 1. A long time ago the territory to NE of Baltimore was controlled by &quot;the Boss,&quot; who were actually two church going mafia style vampires who led a small faction and kept the area secure. They and all their subordinates were hunted and killed on the orders of the Seneschal. The land was left fallow and eventually Ryan (I still don't know his clan) moved in.<br /> <br /> Ryan is a very capable vampire in the older neonate/younger ancilla range, and while he was in the area he was known to keep an eye out for strangers coming into the city. Anyway, I think he abandoned the area because keeping an eye on the bus station by yourself is a crappy job which has been becoming increasingly crappy as more and more vampires have decided to move to Baltimore.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Ryan had decided to present himself to the Reeve and begin the process of gaining citizenship. The bus station (and the whole NE side really) were without (lawful) vampire residents.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm remembering more of what happened as I write this, and as I recall one of the reasons this land is a hot commodity is because the city metro system is expanding is the direction of the LPI. Having a metro station on one's land would make it more valuable. Anyway, we tricked Doris into picking territory which has no direct access to the metro. She was not happy. I wrote about this a few chapters ago.<br /> <br /> So, our plan is to get the bus station shut down and moved to the LPI. Doris had the same idea. The difference was Alice and I figured that it would be a good idea to find out if some other (older) vampire already had domain before we began pulling strings to make it happen. Doris decided to act first and ask questions later.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there was no judgment rendered regarding outside influence on the competition. While it is true that we are involved in a contest to see whose coterie can best develop the barrens into vampire friendly territory, that doesn't necessarily mean it is OK to exert influence on mortal institutions to move strategic assets without the permission of the Prince or Primogen, which was Peter's point.<br /> <br /> But make no mistake, the carthians will certainly have territory in the LPI. The question is how much. Currently, of the five coteries competing in the LPI: 2 are carthian, 1 is invictus, 1 is Ordo Dracul, and 1 is Lancea Sanctum. Further, when the city is considered as a whole the carthians are second only to invictus in territory.<br /> <br /> Also, the contest will not be determined only by personal favorites. This is also an excellent opportunity for the trading of boons. More specifically, for neonates to get into boon debt from elders and ancilla in exchange for assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T12:25:02-07:00","id":902218,"title":"","content":"Personally I don't see why an ancillae would invest into a rigged game if they don't like the predetermined winners, since it just gives ammunition to rivals and it's more efficient to see who gets thrown what and work from there.<br /> <br /> But what happened more recently? I recall you had asked about the requirements regarding the Oath of the Axe back in March or April.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T08:15:54-07:00","id":904972,"title":"","content":"I won't be able to update until after we play next (2 weeks.) There are some unresolved plots that Alice and I are working on, but I try not to write about events in the game until after they resolve so readers do not have to refer back to previous posts more than they already do. <br /> <br /> Regarding the Oath of the Axe: I did start that thread with this game in mind. I have had difficulty as a player choosing what sub-order I eventually want to join. <br /> <br /> Axe: <br /> Alice and I do tend to spend a lot of time ferreting out threats to the city and then doing violence in defense of the city. It is a style of game play that we enjoy. However, while I understand that the description of the Axesworn given in the covenant book is not absolute and their policies must vary from domain to domain; the fact remains that I dislike the idea that there could come a day when I would have to turn a blind ear to a call for help from an NPC that I really like or love (even a family member) because a member of the Ordo Dracul (even one that I really don't care about) is in danger. <br /> <br /> Dying Light: <br /> The idea of roleplaying someone's research assistant for years before becoming a scientist does not particularly appeal to me either. However, members of the dying light are also known for resolving disputes. I very much could see training to become a judge. Some nights I might serve on a juris draconis, and others I could be called on as a judge in the greater city. As a marshal I have served in this capacity for certain minor disputes already. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I think Dying Light will afford us the most freedom as PCs. We will be able to pick our battles rather than having to watch cool NPCs die because we are obligated to defend some random neonate who happens to know a coil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:18:08-07:00","id":905036,"title":"","content":"Awesome, i've always loved to read these, Can't wait for part 9.<br /> <br /> A question though, whats the name of the Prince? So far it hasn't been mentioned yet, while i don't think it would matter if it was never was said figuring how the story has been playing out. What got me curious is to how Kindred outside of Baltimore address the Prince? So do they call the Prince by their name or do they just call him/her by some epithet, like just the Prince of Baltimore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:25:30-07:00","id":905613,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea what the Prince's name is. People in game simply refer to him as the Prince. Or I would imagine if they are from out of town, the Prince of Baltimore. <br /> <br /> Out of character, we call him Dear Leader. We do live in vampire North Korea after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:46:56-07:00","id":911936,"title":"","content":"Wanted to again offer my praise for these write ups. I find this game incredibly engaging and your write ups are top notch. No level of detail is too much, I'm finding every bit fascinating to see. The small details help bring characters to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:30:59-07:00","id":930903,"title":"","content":"Thankyou kindly for the praise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The next chapter is up [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/930902-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-9\">LINK</a>]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}